WEBVTT

00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:40.310
#Encodergasm Presents

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:11.590
Hello, ladies and gentlemen!

00:01:11.590 --> 00:01:12.590
Don't ham it up!

00:01:12.590 --> 00:01:15.670
It's time for the campus festival's main attraction!

00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:16.840
The crowning of the new Miss Countryside!

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:19.430
- Step right up!
- lt's starting, Reese!

00:01:19.430 --> 00:01:20.890
Wait for me, Bertuo!

00:01:20.890 --> 00:01:22.810
The Miss Countryside Contest...

00:01:22.810 --> 00:01:24.560
...accepts contestants from not only our own school...

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:26.060
You're getting cold feet now?

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:29.360
I bet all my
pocket money on you!

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:30.610
85 entered before today...

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:31.610
I won't wear something
like this and be bet on.

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:34.440
... and the remaining 20 will be onstage today for final judging

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:35.440
Hey, nice legs.

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:37.320
Cecily Fairchild!

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:38.410
Hey!

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:42.410
You're an engineering student
who's not even in my classes.

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:46.410
Come on up, Cecily!

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:49.380
I won't have people
betting on me!

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:51.630
But you were nominated!

00:01:51.630 --> 00:01:53.250
Start without her.

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:54.550
Cecily!

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:29.120
That's the army.

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:31.210
What are they doing?

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:41.930
Thanks.

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:44.050
Huh?
There were some tremors?

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:47.560
We're not conducting exercises!

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:50.230
l'll go to the port and check it out!

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:54.150
- Really? Enemies?
- ln the military area!

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:56.230
Talk of enemies now?

00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:57.860
Sounds that way.

00:02:58.570 --> 00:02:59.900
Cecily...

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:02.990
The day I've been
waiting for has arrived.

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:08.000
Are the rumors true?

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:09.580
I think so.

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:11.790
Crossbone Vanguard's
a pirate's name!

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:14.130
No doubt an act of rebellion.

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:16.090
All personnel, evacuate!

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:18.670
The rebel force likely
came prepared!

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:20.880
Resistance is useless!

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:47.740
And this year's
Miss Countryside is...

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:50.790
...Cecily Fairchild!

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:51.830
Me?

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:54.500
But this isn't even
a countryside outfit.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:57.710
Who cares?
You just have to look good!

00:03:57.710 --> 00:04:00.010
- Can it, mechanic!
- Shut up!

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:02.420
Wasn't that
your brother, Reese?

00:04:02.420 --> 00:04:04.340
l don't know that guy!

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:09.600
lt was people like him who voted
for me, so l have no choice but...

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:13.230
- Seabook's not the reason!
- Cecily, l love you!

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:17.730
Look out!

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:26.370
Where are those
mobile suits from?

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:31.750
- Bertuo!
- Cecily!

00:04:37.790 --> 00:04:39.880
We've got to run!

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:41.590
Get down!

00:04:44.510 --> 00:04:45.550
This way!

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:48.010
Get in the evacuation capsules!

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:49.140
He's dead!

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:50.600
T-This boy's...

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:51.600
Dorothy!

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:53.810
Get up! We can't stay here.

00:04:57.350 --> 00:04:59.730
Bertuo! This way!

00:04:59.730 --> 00:05:02.280
- Let us in!
- Sorry, it's full!

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:04.240
l'm heading home!

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:05.780
Cecily!

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:09.660
This is Dwight Camry.

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:11.660
Deputy Commander
Camry, please.

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:13.250
I'm his son!

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:15.080
The line went dead...

00:05:37.310 --> 00:05:39.440
- You!
- Don't fall, you bastard!

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:49.870
l hear there's a war. ls that true?

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:51.950
Grab the survival case, Seabook!

00:05:51.950 --> 00:05:53.290
Right!

00:05:57.330 --> 00:06:00.170
Do you think Mom's
space colony is okay?

00:06:00.170 --> 00:06:02.040
All TV channels are down.

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:03.420
Hey, what's taking you?

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:04.710
Coming!

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:07.090
Let it go!

00:06:11.390 --> 00:06:12.850
Get up!

00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:22.900
We of the Crossbone Vanguard mean no harm to civilians.

00:06:23.270 --> 00:06:25.730
Papa, aren't you back yet?

00:06:25.730 --> 00:06:27.360
Theo!

00:06:28.780 --> 00:06:32.620
Please wait in your evacuation capsules for the time being.

00:06:32.620 --> 00:06:35.700
All this happened because
l wore your dress, Mama!

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:37.500
Papa's a fool, too.

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:47.260
She dumped him, but he's
still carrying a torch for her.

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:52.220
Hey, you people!

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:04.440
- Lady!
- Where's your mom?

00:07:04.440 --> 00:07:07.070
What the hell are
you people doing?

00:07:07.070 --> 00:07:09.700
It's burning!
Call the fire department!

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:11.030
Bertuo, where's your mom?

00:07:11.030 --> 00:07:13.530
- It's windy...
- l can't find her!

00:07:14.070 --> 00:07:16.370
Let's go over to the next block!

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:19.910
Cecily! Arthur!

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:22.080
- Coming!
- Is it safer that way?

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:24.920
Dorothy, there are
mobile suits flying there!

00:07:24.920 --> 00:07:27.590
- Azuma!
- My house!

00:07:27.590 --> 00:07:29.380
Don't cry.

00:07:29.380 --> 00:07:33.140
l wonder if there's a hole
someplace in the colony?

00:07:33.140 --> 00:07:34.930
Maybe.

00:07:34.930 --> 00:07:37.600
Leah, we'll find
your mommy soon.

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:40.020
What army are those guys with?

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:41.640
Here they come!

00:07:45.690 --> 00:07:47.270
Beneath us!

00:08:02.210 --> 00:08:04.750
They're nuts to fight in here!

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:11.880
The Federation Forces
are spreading the fight.

00:08:11.880 --> 00:08:13.840
What a bunch of amateurs!

00:08:22.140 --> 00:08:23.560
Dwight!

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:25.980
This is happening
because idiots...

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:27.310
- Sam! Azuma!
- ...like your old man
are in the military!

00:08:27.310 --> 00:08:28.320
- I'm moving in!
- ...like your old man
are in the military!

00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:31.990
- At least he isn't running away!
- Get off!

00:08:31.990 --> 00:08:33.990
- Dwight, over here!
- Bastard!

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:38.910
Sorry.

00:08:41.950 --> 00:08:43.620
We can't get through here.

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:44.830
Dwight, it's this way?

00:08:44.830 --> 00:08:47.290
- This should be it!
- You sure?

00:08:47.290 --> 00:08:50.670
I heard it from my dad,
so it has to be true!

00:08:50.670 --> 00:08:53.380
- This way, right?
- That's what he says.

00:09:03.270 --> 00:09:04.730
Azuma!

00:09:10.230 --> 00:09:11.860
Mama...

00:09:14.440 --> 00:09:17.360
- Hey, this is a museum!
- You sure about this?

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:19.370
It's in the lobby!

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:23.500
It won't budge!

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:25.960
That's why nobody's
coming this way.

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:28.670
See, l remembered right!

00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:33.260
The enemy's coming...

00:09:33.260 --> 00:09:35.840
Reese, get back! Sam, you too!

00:09:41.890 --> 00:09:43.180
A tank?

00:09:43.180 --> 00:09:45.810
lt's a tank, but it's a mobile suit.

00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:47.940
Don't move from here.

00:09:49.810 --> 00:09:51.230
Oops!

00:09:51.230 --> 00:09:53.900
Don't underestimate us!
Whoever you are!

00:09:53.900 --> 00:09:55.280
- This way!
- Right!

00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:56.780
Dwight!

00:09:58.160 --> 00:09:59.450
Move aside!

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:02.080
Roy Jung, curator of
Roy's War Museum...

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:05.000
...will see to
the defense of this place!

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:07.750
What is that guy piloting?

00:10:07.750 --> 00:10:10.290
Is that weapons
nut General Roy?

00:10:15.630 --> 00:10:18.550
- Get him out of here!
- lt's coming back!

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:21.640
Come on!

00:10:21.640 --> 00:10:23.680
That mobile suit transformed!

00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:25.430
lt's an old tank.

00:10:25.930 --> 00:10:27.730
- Watch the kids!
- What?

00:10:27.730 --> 00:10:30.150
- I'm worried about outside!
- Dorothy!

00:10:30.150 --> 00:10:31.940
This is the shelter!

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:35.780
Shelters have separate
phones lines, right?

00:10:35.780 --> 00:10:38.950
Yeah, we might be
able to call the military!

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:40.990
Azuma! Arthur!

00:10:40.990 --> 00:10:42.620
What are you doing?

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:43.950
C'mon.

00:10:45.410 --> 00:10:48.710
Only death awaits
those who do not fight!

00:10:48.710 --> 00:10:50.960
Sam, is that thing real?

00:10:50.960 --> 00:10:52.130
Okay...

00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:55.550
He says he'll take back the
assembly building with this tank.

00:10:55.550 --> 00:10:58.840
That's a ten year old
transformable mobile suit!

00:10:58.840 --> 00:11:00.550
Arno!

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:02.430
- Do you know Pier 24 on the outer wall?

00:11:02.430 --> 00:11:03.510
- You guys!
- Do you know Pier 24 on the outer wall?

00:11:03.510 --> 00:11:05.180
Yeah.

00:11:05.180 --> 00:11:07.520
An army ship's
waiting for refugees.

00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:09.390
The army top brass is running?

00:11:09.390 --> 00:11:11.060
Looks that way.

00:11:14.560 --> 00:11:15.940
Chris, all ahead!

00:11:15.940 --> 00:11:17.690
Yes, sir!

00:11:17.690 --> 00:11:20.320
lf I don't protect this
space colony, Frontier IV...

00:11:20.320 --> 00:11:23.200
...the museum will
lose its funding!

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:25.830
Do you know where
the launchers are, kids?

00:11:25.830 --> 00:11:28.040
Yeah, the top cover, right?

00:11:28.250 --> 00:11:29.580
Stop!

00:11:29.580 --> 00:11:30.710
You'll get killed!

00:11:30.710 --> 00:11:32.370
Get into the shelter!

00:11:32.370 --> 00:11:35.750
- I'd rather die out there.
- We ought to fight them off.

00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:37.840
Why won't this close?

00:11:37.840 --> 00:11:40.550
l can see the assembly building.

00:11:44.010 --> 00:11:46.560
12 o'clock high, Rohbar!

00:11:55.060 --> 00:11:57.020
- Arthur!
- Don't be stupid!

00:12:07.950 --> 00:12:10.120
Sam, where's Arthur?

00:12:10.120 --> 00:12:11.160
Huh?

00:12:11.160 --> 00:12:13.120
He was on top.
What happened?

00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:14.880
Where's the general?
What's wrong?

00:12:14.880 --> 00:12:17.630
- I don't know.
- We can't use the shelter!

00:12:17.630 --> 00:12:20.260
- General Roy!
- We can't use it?

00:12:20.260 --> 00:12:22.260
I thought you were
going to run away!

00:12:22.590 --> 00:12:24.380
Forget about Arthur!

00:12:24.380 --> 00:12:25.550
But...

00:12:26.140 --> 00:12:30.520
We can get to the outside
of the colony from the shelter.

00:12:30.520 --> 00:12:34.230
That idiot General Roy
trashed the shelter's exit.

00:12:34.230 --> 00:12:38.360
The normal suits, oxygen, and
supplies in there are gone, too.

00:12:44.150 --> 00:12:46.620
Hey! Hey, Arthur!

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:48.620
Arthur! Hey!

00:12:48.620 --> 00:12:51.620
What're you doing,
lying down here?

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:53.210
Hey! Talk to me!

00:12:53.210 --> 00:12:55.830
Stop messing around, Arthur!

00:12:55.830 --> 00:12:57.330
Snap out of it!

00:12:57.330 --> 00:13:00.130
You know we need
a guy like you around!

00:13:00.130 --> 00:13:01.250
Stop it.

00:13:01.250 --> 00:13:03.630
Just let him rest in peace.

00:13:04.220 --> 00:13:05.800
But...

00:13:05.800 --> 00:13:07.550
lt's Arthur...

00:13:13.480 --> 00:13:14.940
Azuma!

00:13:16.020 --> 00:13:19.770
- We can getaway in that tank!
- Seabook's in bad shape...

00:13:19.770 --> 00:13:22.150
Arno, we're leaving.

00:13:22.150 --> 00:13:23.280
Then go.

00:13:23.280 --> 00:13:24.860
Your sister's with us...

00:13:24.860 --> 00:13:26.200
What are you...

00:13:26.780 --> 00:13:28.450
l know!

00:13:28.450 --> 00:13:30.030
l know...

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:35.910
But what the hell is going on?

00:13:35.910 --> 00:13:39.170
Why are two armies
slugging it out here?

00:13:39.840 --> 00:13:44.840
I'm not gonna die just because of
something some adults are doing!

00:13:54.720 --> 00:13:56.100
Ow...

00:13:56.100 --> 00:13:57.310
What're you doing?

00:13:57.310 --> 00:13:58.310
Milk.

00:13:58.310 --> 00:14:00.360
Seabook, aren't you
going too fast?

00:14:00.360 --> 00:14:02.650
The accelerator's sticking!

00:14:02.650 --> 00:14:04.780
Federation soldiers!

00:14:04.780 --> 00:14:06.320
Halt!

00:14:10.820 --> 00:14:12.370
H-Hey, you kids!

00:14:12.370 --> 00:14:13.910
Can we go through?

00:14:13.910 --> 00:14:16.200
Perfect, we'll use this!

00:14:16.710 --> 00:14:19.620
If you want to fight,
give us a hand!

00:14:19.620 --> 00:14:22.920
We just want to get to Pier 24!

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:24.920
Hey, what do you want?

00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:32.510
- Ow!
- What's your problem?

00:14:32.510 --> 00:14:34.810
We must hold the enemy here!

00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:38.270
Hang on, everyone!
l'm backing up!

00:14:39.140 --> 00:14:42.520
They won't attack if
we use children as shields!

00:14:42.520 --> 00:14:44.270
Stop them!

00:14:44.270 --> 00:14:46.190
- What?
- Seabook!

00:14:57.660 --> 00:14:59.460
Use children as shields?

00:14:59.460 --> 00:15:01.000
Are they serious?

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:03.420
Kick those kids out of there!

00:15:05.130 --> 00:15:07.050
Stay away... Stay away!

00:15:07.050 --> 00:15:08.420
Don't!

00:15:08.420 --> 00:15:09.720
Resisting, huh?

00:15:09.720 --> 00:15:11.510
Seize them!

00:15:11.510 --> 00:15:13.600
Not a chance!

00:15:16.180 --> 00:15:17.850
Take out the legs.

00:15:18.180 --> 00:15:20.060
Wait, that voice just now was...

00:15:20.060 --> 00:15:22.310
Cover your ears!

00:15:22.310 --> 00:15:24.900
Is he really gonna do it?

00:15:33.780 --> 00:15:35.740
Where are you headed?

00:15:35.740 --> 00:15:36.740
Dad!

00:15:36.740 --> 00:15:39.410
There's a ship still at Pier 24.

00:15:39.410 --> 00:15:41.960
Make a left at
the next corner then.

00:15:41.960 --> 00:15:43.790
Mr. Arno!

00:15:43.790 --> 00:15:45.170
Thanks.

00:15:45.170 --> 00:15:46.170
Is this all, Sam?

00:15:46.420 --> 00:15:48.670
Arthur was killed...

00:15:49.670 --> 00:15:51.590
My ears are ringing.

00:15:53.340 --> 00:15:55.430
How long will you keep crying?

00:15:55.430 --> 00:15:56.850
Here, Migen.

00:15:57.470 --> 00:16:00.810
It's mineral water
and condensed milk.

00:16:00.810 --> 00:16:04.350
Here you go.
Sorry, l know it's not a nipple.

00:16:04.850 --> 00:16:07.570
You have a baby
who's still breastfeeding?

00:16:07.570 --> 00:16:09.400
Does the right gun pod work?

00:16:09.400 --> 00:16:10.400
Probably.

00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:11.820
Turn left here.

00:16:11.820 --> 00:16:15.280
I think these earrings
Mother left me are ringing...

00:16:15.280 --> 00:16:17.120
Seabook, can we pass?

00:16:17.120 --> 00:16:18.580
Hang on, everyone.

00:16:25.600 --> 00:16:27.790
I think this elevator's working.

00:16:27.790 --> 00:16:29.840
- Does it work?
- Yeah.

00:16:29.840 --> 00:16:32.300
Sam, you don't have
normal suits then?

00:16:32.300 --> 00:16:35.260
Just a few oxygen masks
in the survival case.

00:16:35.260 --> 00:16:38.260
Dorothy, your dad's
going to the pier, right?

00:16:38.260 --> 00:16:41.390
When I called, he was
still at the information bureau.

00:16:41.390 --> 00:16:45.100
Azuma, doesn't the elevator
have any spare normal suits?

00:16:45.100 --> 00:16:47.270
No, this elevator's
for vehicle traffic.

00:16:47.520 --> 00:16:48.650
Oh.

00:16:48.650 --> 00:16:50.910
There should be
some at the pier.

00:16:51.460 --> 00:16:54.040
The ringing is fading...

00:16:55.800 --> 00:16:58.320
What's it like outside, Dad?

00:16:58.320 --> 00:17:01.540
Who's that Crossbone
Vanguard military outfit?

00:17:01.540 --> 00:17:05.010
l heard there were
battleships closing in, too.

00:17:15.320 --> 00:17:17.840
Where are you people headed?

00:17:17.840 --> 00:17:20.430
The ship left a long time ago!

00:17:20.430 --> 00:17:22.390
- Mr. Arno?
- l know.

00:17:22.390 --> 00:17:24.480
Go down another level!

00:17:25.040 --> 00:17:27.950
There should be one
or two space boats.

00:17:31.420 --> 00:17:32.650
You going?

00:17:32.650 --> 00:17:34.150
Let's just forget it!

00:17:34.150 --> 00:17:35.500
Why?

00:17:38.300 --> 00:17:42.740
The Minovsky particles must be
slowing the search for Cecily.

00:17:42.990 --> 00:17:46.410
The top brass
chickened out and ran!

00:17:46.410 --> 00:17:49.630
Wanna make a run
for Frontier llI next door?

00:17:58.280 --> 00:17:59.850
What the hell?

00:18:28.310 --> 00:18:29.830
Let them go.

00:18:29.830 --> 00:18:32.750
Civilians are future
military manpower.

00:18:32.750 --> 00:18:36.050
But those were just
three Jegan types, sir...

00:18:36.050 --> 00:18:39.260
Those running for
their lives can be terrifying.

00:18:39.260 --> 00:18:42.430
- They'll do anything to survive.
- Yes, sir.

00:18:42.430 --> 00:18:44.720
Continue the search
and be alert!

00:18:44.720 --> 00:18:45.890
Yes, sir!

00:18:45.890 --> 00:18:47.440
Any sign of her?

00:18:50.040 --> 00:18:51.400
Here you go!

00:18:57.090 --> 00:18:58.780
Where are you going?

00:18:58.780 --> 00:19:01.700
Don't the explosions
by the elevator worry you?

00:19:01.950 --> 00:19:04.490
Sam, tell my dad to hurry, okay?

00:19:04.490 --> 00:19:05.620
Sure.

00:19:05.620 --> 00:19:08.210
- l'll come, too!
- I'll be fine!

00:19:09.720 --> 00:19:12.380
- Tell him to hurry!
- l know.

00:19:14.480 --> 00:19:17.760
- Make him stop crying!
- l'm trying to!

00:19:17.760 --> 00:19:19.670
Azuma... Are you going out?

00:19:19.920 --> 00:19:22.800
If l have to.
Outside may get rough.

00:19:22.800 --> 00:19:26.270
lf you're sitting,
there's nothing to be afraid of.

00:19:27.160 --> 00:19:29.270
- All done.
- Thanks.

00:19:29.270 --> 00:19:31.140
Dwight, can you handle this?

00:19:31.140 --> 00:19:33.020
It's just like a car, right?

00:19:33.270 --> 00:19:35.150
Get real.

00:19:35.150 --> 00:19:38.510
We did some
training in one once.

00:19:38.510 --> 00:19:41.250
He still can't get the hatch open?

00:19:42.260 --> 00:19:43.870
l wonder what's wrong?

00:19:43.870 --> 00:19:45.740
Good question.

00:19:45.740 --> 00:19:49.580
There's a contact circuit
in front of you to your left.

00:19:49.580 --> 00:19:52.500
A skin-to-skin circuit, huh?

00:19:52.500 --> 00:19:56.680
The power's out, but we
can open the hatch manually.

00:19:57.020 --> 00:19:59.170
What about you, Mr. Arno?

00:19:59.170 --> 00:20:01.670
- Get everyone aboard.
- Sure.

00:20:01.670 --> 00:20:03.520
We can leave soon.

00:20:05.860 --> 00:20:07.470
- Why?
- You know.

00:20:07.470 --> 00:20:09.270
I don't care.

00:20:09.270 --> 00:20:11.230
Cecily? What's going on?

00:20:11.230 --> 00:20:12.560
Don't leave!

00:20:12.560 --> 00:20:14.990
Just forget about your friends!

00:20:15.540 --> 00:20:19.530
What are you doing?
lf you fire again, so will l!

00:20:19.750 --> 00:20:21.280
Stay out of this!

00:20:21.280 --> 00:20:23.450
This is family business!

00:20:25.220 --> 00:20:27.080
Parents don't point
guns at their kids.

00:20:27.330 --> 00:20:29.040
Shut up!

00:20:29.890 --> 00:20:31.460
No!

00:20:33.430 --> 00:20:35.010
Please stop!

00:20:37.690 --> 00:20:39.100
Bastard...

00:20:41.400 --> 00:20:42.510
Don't go!

00:20:42.510 --> 00:20:43.630
Why not?

00:20:43.630 --> 00:20:45.970
You just shot my friend!

00:20:45.970 --> 00:20:49.260
Think about why I had you
wear your mother's earrings.

00:20:49.260 --> 00:20:51.520
This is a special day!

00:20:53.120 --> 00:20:54.230
Seabook!

00:20:54.230 --> 00:20:55.690
Cecily, don't!

00:20:57.310 --> 00:20:59.030
No!

00:21:00.580 --> 00:21:02.330
Stay away!

00:21:22.190 --> 00:21:23.590
Lord Dorel.

00:21:23.590 --> 00:21:27.970
This didn't go according
to plan, Theo Fairchild.

00:21:27.970 --> 00:21:29.810
No, sir.

00:21:30.160 --> 00:21:33.310
- This is my younger sister?
- Yes, sir.

00:21:37.250 --> 00:21:38.900
Don't be afraid.

00:21:38.900 --> 00:21:42.870
Your brother came
in person to take you home.

00:21:44.920 --> 00:21:46.870
Take me home?

00:21:47.420 --> 00:21:49.370
Why? Tell me why!

00:21:49.370 --> 00:21:52.450
The Ronah family
has need of you.

00:21:52.450 --> 00:21:56.370
l'm merely carrying out
our grandfather's wishes.

00:21:56.370 --> 00:21:57.620
Take me home?

00:21:57.620 --> 00:21:58.370
Grandfather?

00:21:58.620 --> 00:22:01.040
We can't afford to relax yet.

00:22:01.040 --> 00:22:02.350
Please hurry.

00:22:04.020 --> 00:22:05.510
Dorel Ronah?

00:22:05.510 --> 00:22:07.010
Yes.

00:22:07.010 --> 00:22:09.340
But without Mother's approval...

00:22:09.590 --> 00:22:11.430
What are you saying?

00:22:11.430 --> 00:22:15.220
lt is because Theo there
let your mother escape...

00:22:15.220 --> 00:22:17.640
...that her whereabouts
remain unknown.

00:22:17.640 --> 00:22:19.850
To search for her...

00:22:19.850 --> 00:22:23.480
...would it not be wise
to join the Crossbone Vanguard?

00:22:23.480 --> 00:22:26.700
I'm going home for that?

00:22:30.970 --> 00:22:34.740
May I have the honor of seeing
her once she has settled in?

00:22:34.740 --> 00:22:38.500
The Ronah family never forgets
a debt to an adoptive parent.

00:22:38.750 --> 00:22:40.800
Thank you, lord.

00:23:01.400 --> 00:23:03.360
Seabook!

00:23:04.620 --> 00:23:06.820
Are you okay?

00:23:06.820 --> 00:23:10.290
Reese, get me some
scissors and antiseptic.

00:23:11.550 --> 00:23:13.320
What're you doing?

00:23:13.320 --> 00:23:15.460
Sit down, everybody.

00:23:16.590 --> 00:23:18.620
Sam, where's my dad?

00:23:18.620 --> 00:23:21.000
He's out opening the hatch.

00:23:21.000 --> 00:23:22.380
l see...

00:23:24.600 --> 00:23:26.920
Buckle up, everybody!

00:23:26.920 --> 00:23:29.340
Azuma, you can
see Mr. Arno, right?

00:23:29.340 --> 00:23:30.760
Yeah, I'll tell you when.

00:23:31.010 --> 00:23:33.180
It'll be open in a second, Azuma.

00:23:33.180 --> 00:23:35.300
Right, whenever you're ready!

00:23:35.300 --> 00:23:37.600
l'm undocking us!

00:23:37.600 --> 00:23:38.640
Too soon!

00:23:38.640 --> 00:23:40.530
- l'm doing it right!
- Ow!

00:23:53.970 --> 00:23:55.710
Mr. Arno!

00:24:06.640 --> 00:24:08.960
Do it gently!

00:24:08.960 --> 00:24:10.300
Hang in there!

00:24:10.300 --> 00:24:11.510
I'm trying!

00:24:11.510 --> 00:24:12.810
Ow!

00:24:17.320 --> 00:24:21.190
Look at how much
of our town's on fire!

00:24:22.700 --> 00:24:26.860
lt's hard to tell from 6000 m, but
judging by those smoke trails...

00:24:27.110 --> 00:24:30.240
...there's probably a hole
in the colony somewhere.

00:24:39.840 --> 00:24:43.330
- What's going on?
- There's a hole in the colony!

00:24:44.180 --> 00:24:46.090
Are we gonna be destroyed?

00:25:04.910 --> 00:25:08.610
l said I won't commit suicide,
and you're still there?

00:25:08.610 --> 00:25:11.030
Yes, we will remain...

00:25:11.030 --> 00:25:14.950
...until you are presented
to your father and grandfather.

00:25:15.380 --> 00:25:19.200
My name is Cecily Fairchild.

00:25:19.200 --> 00:25:21.040
Not Berah Ronah.

00:25:21.040 --> 00:25:25.330
Nevertheless, you are the eldest
daughter of the Ronah family...

00:25:25.330 --> 00:25:27.920
...proponents of
the Cosmo Aristocracy.

00:25:27.920 --> 00:25:31.800
You will grow used to being
waited upon by your inferiors.

00:25:31.800 --> 00:25:35.590
This is but one of
the duties of the highborn.

00:25:35.590 --> 00:25:37.690
- Duty?
- Yes, lady.

00:25:41.660 --> 00:25:44.060
- l'm to change into this?
- Yes.

00:25:44.060 --> 00:25:46.480
All right. l'll do it myself.

00:25:46.480 --> 00:25:49.450
No, lady, please allow us to help.

00:25:51.460 --> 00:25:53.120
This way, please.

00:26:00.720 --> 00:26:04.160
- But it's the middle of autumn...
- Yes, lady.

00:26:04.160 --> 00:26:06.160
The weather control computer...

00:26:06.160 --> 00:26:09.170
...is failing due to our
air raid, according to rumors.

00:26:09.420 --> 00:26:10.970
It's no rumor.

00:26:32.330 --> 00:26:37.340
maru de kanashimi no kakera da wa
Almost like shards of sorrow...

00:26:37.340 --> 00:26:42.740
machi wo tozasu garasu iro no yuki
...glass-colored snow hems the town in.

00:26:42.740 --> 00:26:48.040
ashita wo sagasu hitomi sae mo
Even eyes that search for tomorrow...

00:26:48.040 --> 00:26:53.090
kumorasete yuku no yami no kanata
...are dimmed by the depths of the darkness.

00:26:53.090 --> 00:26:58.190
mishiranu chikara ni nagasarete
Being swept along by an unfamiliar power...

00:26:58.190 --> 00:27:03.530
kokoro ga dokoka e hagureteku
...the heart is led astray somewhere.

00:27:03.530 --> 00:27:08.520
harisakesou na mune no oku de
Deep within this heart that seems fit to burst...

00:27:08.520 --> 00:27:15.200
kodou dake ga tashika ni ikite iru
...it's only the throbbing that is surely alive.

00:27:16.670 --> 00:27:21.410
hikaru kaze no naka
Within the shining wind...

00:27:21.410 --> 00:27:27.160
kikoete kuru anata no koe
...l can hear your voice.

00:27:27.160 --> 00:27:31.830
Pray don't break our peace forever...

00:27:31.830 --> 00:27:39.930
sono kagayaki wo shinjite iru
...l believe in that brilliance.

00:28:00.840 --> 00:28:03.160
I'm glad you're safe, Lady Berah.

00:28:03.160 --> 00:28:07.000
My congratulations
on your homecoming.

00:28:10.810 --> 00:28:12.540
Don't you realize...

00:28:12.540 --> 00:28:16.590
...that even Mother started
to hate you because of all this?

00:28:16.590 --> 00:28:19.130
It couldn't be helped.

00:28:19.130 --> 00:28:20.470
lt couldn't.

00:28:27.950 --> 00:28:31.890
This is the man who eloped
with Mother, bringing me along?

00:28:31.890 --> 00:28:34.570
Lady Berah, come in.

00:28:35.040 --> 00:28:37.910
Your father is waiting for you.

00:28:44.090 --> 00:28:46.660
You saw the battle's
progress outside.

00:28:46.660 --> 00:28:49.120
It's good of you
to come, though you...

00:28:49.120 --> 00:28:50.420
Berah!

00:28:51.750 --> 00:28:53.960
Surely you remember my voice.

00:28:53.960 --> 00:28:56.250
lt's me. lt's Carozzo.

00:28:56.250 --> 00:28:58.590
Then take off that mask.

00:29:00.060 --> 00:29:05.300
l'm a pathetic man who lost
his wife to that man, Theo.

00:29:05.300 --> 00:29:10.350
I also swore to bring the ideals of
your grandfather Meitzer to life.

00:29:10.350 --> 00:29:15.310
That day, l began my
struggle against my weak side...

00:29:15.310 --> 00:29:17.980
...and I became as
you see me now.

00:29:17.980 --> 00:29:20.860
That speaking style,
that stubbornness...

00:29:20.860 --> 00:29:23.400
They could only
come from my father.

00:29:23.400 --> 00:29:28.530
But why can't you admit Mother
had no choice but to leave you...

00:29:28.530 --> 00:29:30.210
...since she couldn't
accept them?

00:29:30.890 --> 00:29:34.210
l see Nadia told you a great deal.

00:29:34.540 --> 00:29:38.300
I don't intend
to be like this forever.

00:29:38.730 --> 00:29:41.380
In fact, l have forgiven Theo...

00:29:41.380 --> 00:29:45.930
...and have met you in spite
of my unbearable shame.

00:29:45.930 --> 00:29:48.550
Is that why you need that mask?

00:29:48.550 --> 00:29:50.440
l suppose it is.

00:29:53.910 --> 00:29:57.140
I swore that I wouldn't
take off this mask...

00:29:57.140 --> 00:30:00.690
...until Cosmo
Babylonia is founded.

00:30:00.690 --> 00:30:01.940
Forgive me.

00:30:01.940 --> 00:30:04.110
Cosmo Babylonia?

00:30:04.110 --> 00:30:05.440
What's that?

00:30:05.440 --> 00:30:09.070
Our thousand year dream...

00:30:09.070 --> 00:30:11.830
...for the eternal
survival of humanity.

00:30:11.830 --> 00:30:14.910
- Dream?
- lt's been ten years.

00:30:14.910 --> 00:30:17.830
I'm sure your grandfather
is anxious to see you.

00:30:17.830 --> 00:30:19.120
l'll take you.

00:30:19.120 --> 00:30:21.880
ls he here on Frontier IV?

00:30:21.880 --> 00:30:25.380
This colony is
no longer Frontier IV.

00:30:25.380 --> 00:30:28.270
lt is Babylon, Cosmo Babylon.

00:30:53.880 --> 00:30:56.500
The reason l called you here...

00:30:57.010 --> 00:31:00.500
...is that until Cosmo
Babylonia is established...

00:31:00.500 --> 00:31:03.840
...l'd like you to act as our queen.

00:31:03.840 --> 00:31:05.510
Act as queen?

00:31:06.230 --> 00:31:10.020
The masses always
demand an idol.

00:31:10.570 --> 00:31:13.300
Having lived and
worked among them...

00:31:13.300 --> 00:31:15.350
...you have that idol's charm.

00:31:15.350 --> 00:31:16.470
But that's...

00:31:16.470 --> 00:31:18.440
l could never...

00:31:19.620 --> 00:31:23.610
l could never do
something so outrageous.

00:31:23.610 --> 00:31:27.400
I was so happy that
I got ahead of myself.

00:31:27.400 --> 00:31:29.360
Forgive me, Berah.

00:31:29.360 --> 00:31:31.040
Grandfather...

00:31:31.760 --> 00:31:34.830
Forgive me for
thinking only of myself.

00:31:41.390 --> 00:31:46.210
From this blood, you can't tell if
the person sitting here died, right?

00:31:46.210 --> 00:31:49.300
This area saw
a good deal of combat.

00:31:49.300 --> 00:31:52.380
We even lost two
of our mobile suits.

00:31:52.380 --> 00:31:55.440
There are still air leaks, as well.

00:31:55.950 --> 00:31:57.220
We should hurry.

00:31:57.220 --> 00:31:58.860
I understand.

00:32:03.790 --> 00:32:05.650
Seabook...

00:32:05.900 --> 00:32:09.200
What should l do?

00:32:17.870 --> 00:32:20.370
Frontier Side's Federation fleet...

00:32:20.370 --> 00:32:22.710
...has all been
chased to Frontier Il?

00:32:22.710 --> 00:32:26.130
Yes, but it's a matter of time
before we drive them out.

00:32:26.130 --> 00:32:27.170
I suppose.

00:32:27.170 --> 00:32:30.840
Then comes the job of
mopping up the colonies.

00:32:30.840 --> 00:32:32.340
White Sox launching.

00:32:32.340 --> 00:32:34.680
Roger, don't die on us, you hear?

00:32:34.680 --> 00:32:36.850
Do you even need to ask?

00:32:56.380 --> 00:33:00.580
When you're near the colony,
don't blow the main engine.

00:33:00.580 --> 00:33:04.620
This colony will be one of
Cosmo Babylonia's new worlds.

00:33:04.620 --> 00:33:05.880
Yes, sir!

00:33:07.140 --> 00:33:10.750
Don't touch those Colony
Public Corporation people.

00:33:10.750 --> 00:33:13.890
Our only enemies are
the Earth Federation Forces!

00:33:14.440 --> 00:33:16.230
Here they come!

00:33:18.900 --> 00:33:21.150
S-Squadron leader!

00:33:38.200 --> 00:33:41.000
Let's get out of here, everyone!

00:33:43.970 --> 00:33:45.420
Taters.

00:33:46.060 --> 00:33:47.620
What happened here?

00:33:47.620 --> 00:33:48.930
What?

00:33:49.640 --> 00:33:50.790
It's a Federation ship!

00:33:50.790 --> 00:33:52.140
What's it doing?

00:33:57.070 --> 00:33:58.470
You bastards!

00:33:58.470 --> 00:34:00.650
There's gravity here!

00:34:01.410 --> 00:34:03.520
At this rate, we'll...

00:34:04.240 --> 00:34:07.360
- Brace us with the arm!
- Y-Yes, ma'am!

00:34:08.850 --> 00:34:11.440
- Damn it...
- Go, Manuela!

00:34:11.440 --> 00:34:14.610
At this rate, before we even
fight the Crossbone Vanguard...

00:34:14.610 --> 00:34:15.990
...we'll end up dead!

00:34:15.990 --> 00:34:18.530
Begging the colonel's pardon...

00:34:18.530 --> 00:34:21.490
...but all my instructor
pilots are out.

00:34:21.490 --> 00:34:24.160
With my NCOs and
officers out fighting...

00:34:24.160 --> 00:34:28.290
...we were the only ones left
to pilot this ship to Frontier l.

00:34:28.290 --> 00:34:32.590
That's why I said to use this
training ship as a resistance base!

00:34:32.590 --> 00:34:34.210
The enemy'll come soon.

00:34:34.210 --> 00:34:37.260
Make sure we can
use the F91 , understood?

00:34:37.260 --> 00:34:38.430
Where are you going?

00:34:38.430 --> 00:34:40.690
To bring resistance groups here!

00:34:45.870 --> 00:34:47.640
Who the hell are you?

00:34:47.640 --> 00:34:50.480
If you have time to run,
fight in the Space Ark!

00:34:50.480 --> 00:34:52.520
We're just kids, mister.

00:34:52.520 --> 00:34:54.820
lf you can fly this boat,
you can fight!

00:34:54.820 --> 00:34:55.860
Go!

00:34:55.860 --> 00:34:58.540
Hey, I was on my way down!

00:34:59.360 --> 00:35:01.120
There you go!

00:35:02.630 --> 00:35:04.040
Got it!

00:35:11.600 --> 00:35:12.970
Seabook!

00:35:20.610 --> 00:35:23.010
- W-We've got him!
- Leah, let go!

00:35:23.010 --> 00:35:24.690
- Ow...
- Pull!

00:35:25.490 --> 00:35:27.060
Thanks.

00:35:29.240 --> 00:35:32.600
- Sorry about that.
- Dorothy's got fast reflexes.

00:35:32.600 --> 00:35:33.730
Lucky shot.

00:35:33.730 --> 00:35:36.570
But can we really
hide the ship with this?

00:35:36.570 --> 00:35:39.110
lt'll look like rocks
or trees far away.

00:35:39.110 --> 00:35:39.950
Oh.

00:35:40.110 --> 00:35:42.780
Close this up after you eat.

00:35:42.780 --> 00:35:45.700
We're working inside,
so we don't want light to show.

00:35:45.910 --> 00:35:46.330
- Roger!

00:35:46.330 --> 00:35:47.290
- Yes, Chief Petty Officer Roos!
- Roger!

00:35:47.290 --> 00:35:47.790
- Yes, Chief Petty Officer Roos!

00:35:48.040 --> 00:35:48.750
- Yes, Chief Petty Officer Roos!
- Don't run around!

00:35:48.750 --> 00:35:49.870
- Don't run around!

00:35:49.870 --> 00:35:51.460
Control those kids.

00:35:51.460 --> 00:35:53.630
Don't look at me,
they're not my kids.

00:35:53.630 --> 00:35:55.590
That was delicious.

00:35:55.590 --> 00:35:56.460
Seabook!

00:35:56.670 --> 00:36:00.010
If that wound's healed,
you don't need the sling.

00:36:00.010 --> 00:36:01.130
It hurts a bit.

00:36:01.130 --> 00:36:03.390
Come on,
it's not gonna kill you.

00:36:04.360 --> 00:36:07.430
Acting Captain Leahlee!
Hey, it's on.

00:36:08.370 --> 00:36:09.930
She has every right.

00:36:09.930 --> 00:36:13.100
She took the helm and
snuck us into this colony.

00:36:13.100 --> 00:36:14.400
ls that from Earth?

00:36:14.610 --> 00:36:17.360
Yeah, the top brass
are all on vacation.

00:36:17.360 --> 00:36:20.740
Frontier Side is the newest
residential colony cluster, right?

00:36:20.940 --> 00:36:25.570
lt's like two drunks in a brawl.
We'll wait until it quiets down.

00:36:25.570 --> 00:36:26.830
What?

00:36:26.830 --> 00:36:28.490
lf that's the official stance...

00:36:28.490 --> 00:36:32.090
Are they saying the Crossbone
Vanguard's some kind ofjoke?

00:36:34.730 --> 00:36:38.170
You know, l used to wonder...

00:36:38.170 --> 00:36:42.090
...why our colony's
towns are so classical...

00:36:42.090 --> 00:36:45.180
...but after seeing the Crossbone
Vanguard, I think l know.

00:36:45.180 --> 00:36:47.020
What do you mean?

00:36:47.570 --> 00:36:50.810
Maybe somebody in
the Federation government...

00:36:50.810 --> 00:36:54.230
...or the Colony Public Corp.
is conspiring with the Crossbone.

00:36:54.440 --> 00:36:57.860
- That's a real possibility.
- Wow, what a babe!

00:36:58.620 --> 00:37:03.490
Can you take this to Gruce?
He's working on a mobile suit.

00:37:03.490 --> 00:37:04.830
Sure.

00:37:08.300 --> 00:37:10.790
Here's your dinner, Gruce.

00:37:10.990 --> 00:37:12.450
Just leave it there.

00:37:12.450 --> 00:37:14.620
Did you hear
the broadcast from Earth?

00:37:14.620 --> 00:37:19.380
The guys on Earth know that
the Crossbone won't attack them.

00:37:19.380 --> 00:37:28.850
Circuit three connects here to NSS-23 and green connector 48...

00:37:21.310 --> 00:37:22.550
What's this?

00:37:22.550 --> 00:37:23.550
The repair manual.

00:37:23.800 --> 00:37:25.090
Really?

00:37:25.090 --> 00:37:26.020
Yeah, the F91 's an unfinished
prototype with nice features...

00:37:28.850 --> 00:37:31.680
...so I have to adjust it
every time it's sent out.

00:37:31.680 --> 00:37:34.060
Hand typed from
a word processor?

00:37:34.060 --> 00:37:37.060
We don't even
have all the pages.

00:37:37.060 --> 00:37:39.360
- Show that at normal speed.
- W-Why?

00:37:39.360 --> 00:37:41.070
That's my mom!

00:37:39.870 --> 00:37:42.230
I don't believe this will ever occur...

00:37:41.070 --> 00:37:42.230
Dr. Arno?

00:37:42.230 --> 00:37:43.660
Yeah...

00:37:42.230 --> 00:37:44.280
... but just in case the connection is ever broken...

00:37:44.280 --> 00:37:48.340
She said she wanted to research
bio-computers and left home...

00:37:48.340 --> 00:37:52.040
...but she was really working
on mobile suit development?

00:37:52.040 --> 00:37:53.040
Look at this.

00:37:53.040 --> 00:37:54.710
Hey, you're her kid...

00:37:54.710 --> 00:37:58.540
...so maybe you know what
Dr. Arno's talking about.

00:37:58.540 --> 00:38:02.210
How could I understand
something that complicated?

00:38:02.210 --> 00:38:05.720
Don't tell my sister
about that manual!

00:38:30.820 --> 00:38:31.990
Close shutters!

00:38:31.990 --> 00:38:33.540
Transfer to the combat bridge!

00:38:33.790 --> 00:38:36.330
lt's up to you, mobile suit team!

00:38:36.330 --> 00:38:38.260
30 degrees down!

00:38:38.810 --> 00:38:41.000
The Crossbone
leaders should be...

00:38:41.000 --> 00:38:43.960
...in the government office or
the guest palace, so hit those!

00:38:43.960 --> 00:38:47.630
There are probably thousands
of refugees camped near there.

00:38:47.630 --> 00:38:51.730
That's a small enough
price to pay to end this war!

00:39:04.150 --> 00:39:05.690
Ship barrage!

00:39:05.690 --> 00:39:08.240
Aren't they targeting
the guest palace?

00:39:12.880 --> 00:39:14.160
Lady Berah.

00:39:14.160 --> 00:39:15.580
Turn out the lights.

00:39:15.580 --> 00:39:16.910
lt's already dawn.

00:39:16.910 --> 00:39:18.420
Yes, lady.

00:39:19.100 --> 00:39:21.630
An attack from space under our feet...

00:39:20.250 --> 00:39:21.630
ls everything all right?

00:39:22.630 --> 00:39:23.630
Everything is fine!

00:39:23.790 --> 00:39:25.670
Don't stay near the Ronahs.

00:39:25.670 --> 00:39:27.010
Mom! Mom!

00:39:27.010 --> 00:39:30.630
This place will be
a sitting duck for the Feds!

00:39:30.630 --> 00:39:32.340
Your Excellency!

00:39:32.340 --> 00:39:33.970
Grandfather...

00:39:33.970 --> 00:39:37.810
You should hurry and
make plans to escape, Berah.

00:39:37.810 --> 00:39:42.600
ln an attack like this, there may
not be time to prepare, so l didn't.

00:39:42.770 --> 00:39:47.660
So you must sometimes
hand yourself over to fate?

00:39:48.170 --> 00:39:49.860
You're right...

00:39:49.860 --> 00:39:54.200
You just roll the dice
and accept the outcome.

00:39:54.200 --> 00:39:57.410
The next beam could
come from under our feet...

00:39:57.410 --> 00:40:01.080
...vaporizing both our bodies.

00:40:01.080 --> 00:40:03.290
lf that happens,
forgive me, Berah.

00:40:03.290 --> 00:40:05.840
N-No, that's all right...

00:40:05.840 --> 00:40:09.710
Ever since Mother fled the family,
I've become used to it.

00:40:09.710 --> 00:40:12.010
l'm relieved to hear that.

00:40:12.220 --> 00:40:14.970
When l launched
the attack on this colony...

00:40:14.970 --> 00:40:19.220
...l wouldn't let the Crossbone
Vanguard harm a single civilian.

00:40:19.220 --> 00:40:22.230
But the Federation
soldiers would.

00:40:22.230 --> 00:40:25.730
That's the true face of
an absolute democracy's army.

00:40:25.730 --> 00:40:29.030
Without a cause to follow,
when they see change...

00:40:29.030 --> 00:40:31.570
...they follow it blindly.

00:40:31.570 --> 00:40:35.200
You're saying that's the result
of the popular revolution.

00:40:35.200 --> 00:40:36.500
Yes.

00:40:37.880 --> 00:40:40.910
Anyway, people started
living in space...

00:40:40.910 --> 00:40:45.000
...as the price they
paid for destroying nature.

00:40:45.000 --> 00:40:49.630
But now that space
life is common...

00:40:49.630 --> 00:40:52.390
...people are returning to Earth.

00:40:53.440 --> 00:40:56.930
But those are only
the elite of the Federation.

00:40:56.930 --> 00:41:00.690
Ordinary citizens aren't
permitted to return.

00:41:01.370 --> 00:41:02.810
You aren't cold?

00:41:02.810 --> 00:41:04.060
No.

00:41:07.910 --> 00:41:10.110
It's gotten so quiet...

00:41:10.110 --> 00:41:11.150
Yes.

00:41:11.150 --> 00:41:15.360
The Crossbone Vanguard your
father Carozzo created is amazing.

00:41:15.570 --> 00:41:16.820
My father?

00:41:17.030 --> 00:41:21.670
But Earth's rebirth
will take a long time.

00:41:22.220 --> 00:41:26.790
Man must make his home
here in space forever.

00:41:26.790 --> 00:41:28.340
I-I see.

00:41:28.590 --> 00:41:30.050
Despite that...

00:41:30.050 --> 00:41:34.170
...those who returned to Earth
have long maintained a policy...

00:41:34.170 --> 00:41:36.840
...of abandoning
those they left behind.

00:41:36.840 --> 00:41:41.180
But the Cosmo Aristocracy you
advocate also discriminates...

00:41:41.390 --> 00:41:45.310
Highborns have duties
that they must fulfill.

00:41:45.310 --> 00:41:46.390
Of course.

00:41:46.390 --> 00:41:49.110
For instance,
on the battlefield, a commoner...

00:41:49.310 --> 00:41:51.980
...can say he's afraid and run.

00:41:51.980 --> 00:41:56.740
But a noble, a man of renown,
must stand his ground and fight...

00:41:56.740 --> 00:41:59.160
...unafraid of his spilt blood.

00:41:59.160 --> 00:42:01.210
People aren't equal?

00:42:01.800 --> 00:42:06.460
Their human rights are equal,
but no two people are the same.

00:42:06.460 --> 00:42:10.290
So men and the world should
be ruled by the highborn.

00:42:10.290 --> 00:42:15.570
By those unafraid
to spill their own blood.

00:42:15.570 --> 00:42:22.180
When l was young,
you often told me stories like that.

00:42:22.180 --> 00:42:26.430
But it was Mother who was
crushed by those principles.

00:42:26.430 --> 00:42:29.900
l was too strict with Nadia.

00:42:29.900 --> 00:42:34.030
It made her abandon
everything nobility holds dear.

00:42:34.030 --> 00:42:36.950
I'm my mother's daughter.

00:42:49.100 --> 00:42:52.140
That's what you get for
not watching your step!

00:42:52.690 --> 00:42:57.260
Who's the one who left
the deck tilted in the fog?

00:42:57.470 --> 00:42:59.130
Why a Heavygun?

00:42:59.130 --> 00:43:02.600
We're not rolling in
mobile suits here, you know!

00:43:02.600 --> 00:43:05.180
Don't play with the live ammo!

00:43:08.950 --> 00:43:12.240
You made the mess,
so you'll clean it up.

00:43:13.980 --> 00:43:16.530
They should be
shipped off to camp!

00:43:16.530 --> 00:43:18.070
My thoughts exactly.

00:43:18.070 --> 00:43:19.400
Minmi, handle it!

00:43:19.400 --> 00:43:21.040
Yes, sir!

00:43:22.720 --> 00:43:24.530
Leah, l need that milk!

00:43:24.530 --> 00:43:25.580
It's coming!

00:43:25.580 --> 00:43:27.040
A baby, too...

00:43:27.040 --> 00:43:28.620
l know!

00:43:28.620 --> 00:43:32.290
- Reese, do you know...
- You're such a bastard!

00:43:32.290 --> 00:43:36.760
I thought I told you not to tell
my sister about our mom!

00:43:36.760 --> 00:43:40.550
She can deal with her emotional
problems once the war's over!

00:43:40.550 --> 00:43:44.550
Do you have any idea what it's
like for kids who just managed...

00:43:44.550 --> 00:43:46.310
...to forget about their mother?

00:43:46.310 --> 00:43:47.810
Bastard!

00:43:47.810 --> 00:43:49.430
- Cosmo!
- You're terrible!

00:43:49.430 --> 00:43:52.650
If you keep this up, I won't
tell you what Mom meant!

00:43:52.810 --> 00:43:56.270
What?
You understand that code?

00:43:56.270 --> 00:43:59.070
That's no code.

00:44:00.450 --> 00:44:02.820
Don't worry, Seabook.

00:44:02.820 --> 00:44:07.590
l think I understand what
kind of person Mom is now.

00:44:08.300 --> 00:44:09.870
Really?

00:44:09.870 --> 00:44:16.090
Mom didn't leave home
because she hated us or Dad.

00:44:16.900 --> 00:44:20.640
l could tell that from
the video Gruce showed me.

00:44:21.820 --> 00:44:22.970
Wow...

00:44:22.970 --> 00:44:26.350
Adults have lots of
things they have to do.

00:44:27.410 --> 00:44:31.390
Reese, you understand
that code where she said...

00:44:31.390 --> 00:44:33.350
..."open 8 columns,
make a bridge"?

00:44:33.600 --> 00:44:35.110
It's no code.

00:44:36.460 --> 00:44:37.820
- Look.
- A cat's cradle?

00:44:38.020 --> 00:44:40.490
Is "cat's cradle" the password?

00:44:40.490 --> 00:44:43.450
ls it those circuits in the F91 ?

00:44:44.970 --> 00:44:47.380
This was Mom's specialty.

00:44:52.220 --> 00:44:54.670
An 8-column bridge.

00:44:54.670 --> 00:44:58.710
That's it! The top surface is
the hard computer's panel face!

00:44:58.710 --> 00:45:03.050
And the lines leading down are
the bio-computer's parallel circuits?

00:45:03.050 --> 00:45:04.590
Right! Of course!

00:45:04.590 --> 00:45:06.980
Like mother, like daughter!

00:45:09.200 --> 00:45:12.100
So we'll be able
to use the F91 , right?

00:45:12.100 --> 00:45:16.100
You have pilots in your
resistance group, right?

00:45:16.100 --> 00:45:18.190
We have engineering students.

00:45:18.190 --> 00:45:20.020
One of you can do it!

00:45:20.020 --> 00:45:20.900
You're serious?

00:45:21.070 --> 00:45:23.900
Those pirate Crossbone
Vanguard bastards...

00:45:23.900 --> 00:45:26.700
...trashed an entire colony!

00:45:26.700 --> 00:45:30.290
lf you don't want your sister killed
and tossed into cold space...

00:45:30.290 --> 00:45:31.580
...you'll pilot it!

00:45:31.580 --> 00:45:32.750
There's no reason to fight.

00:45:32.910 --> 00:45:35.120
That's an order! Got it?

00:45:35.120 --> 00:45:36.620
Really, is that so?

00:45:36.620 --> 00:45:39.130
Can he pilot a mobile suit?

00:45:39.130 --> 00:45:41.170
- Don't let him push you.
- Yeah.

00:45:41.170 --> 00:45:44.670
Still, your old lady
designed its bio-computer.

00:45:44.840 --> 00:45:47.010
You might be a good fit.

00:45:47.010 --> 00:45:49.680
lf you're a Newtype, that is.

00:45:49.680 --> 00:45:51.180
What's a Newtype?

00:45:51.180 --> 00:45:54.180
Someone with
natural piloting abilities.

00:45:54.180 --> 00:45:55.640
Are you really okay?

00:45:55.640 --> 00:45:59.610
l was glad when
I saw Mom was talking...

00:45:59.610 --> 00:46:03.530
...about cat's cradles on
that video, just like she used to.

00:46:03.530 --> 00:46:05.200
I see.

00:46:05.200 --> 00:46:08.370
Maybe Mom touched
this mobile suit.

00:46:09.220 --> 00:46:11.130
Yeah, that's true!

00:46:19.810 --> 00:46:21.040
Well done.

00:46:21.040 --> 00:46:23.960
l see you've already
mastered the basics.

00:46:23.960 --> 00:46:26.470
lt has nothing to do with my skill.

00:46:26.470 --> 00:46:30.640
I just sensed that the mobile
suit has a delicate feel.

00:46:30.640 --> 00:46:37.060
If you feel that way,
you're a natural.

00:46:37.060 --> 00:46:39.440
It's not that simple!

00:46:39.440 --> 00:46:44.110
Our sortie was delayed 1 0
minutes for a single trainee?

00:46:44.110 --> 00:46:45.440
Who is she?

00:46:45.440 --> 00:46:47.950
A direct heir to
the Ronah family.

00:46:47.950 --> 00:46:50.070
I haven't seen
Dorel since last night.

00:46:50.070 --> 00:46:52.580
He's in an operation on Frontier I.

00:46:52.780 --> 00:46:54.910
Our recon takes us pretty far.

00:46:54.910 --> 00:46:56.210
Yes, ma'am!

00:46:58.850 --> 00:47:03.670
A trainee who gets Lieutenant
Zabine's personal attention?

00:47:03.670 --> 00:47:05.680
- Move it!
- Yes, ma'am!

00:47:15.660 --> 00:47:18.730
The Federation's
resistance forces are quick.

00:47:18.730 --> 00:47:20.810
Does this mean they know...

00:47:20.810 --> 00:47:24.450
...that we won't destroy Frontier I
because it's a resource colony?

00:47:42.140 --> 00:47:44.960
If we go straight through here...

00:47:44.960 --> 00:47:46.920
...we should be inside Frontier l.

00:47:47.090 --> 00:47:50.470
But wasn't the goal just
to gain control of these caves?

00:47:50.630 --> 00:47:52.060
l know that!

00:47:52.570 --> 00:47:56.610
If we have energy, we should
scout for the next mission.

00:48:04.110 --> 00:48:06.520
But we'd be disobeying orders!

00:48:06.520 --> 00:48:09.900
The mop-up comes after
the Babylonia Declaration!

00:48:09.900 --> 00:48:13.820
Enough, only those loyal
to me should come then.

00:48:13.820 --> 00:48:15.750
Open the inner hatch.

00:48:24.580 --> 00:48:27.340
- Hey!
- Okay, back to port.

00:48:27.340 --> 00:48:28.920
Our hull isn't tough.

00:48:28.920 --> 00:48:30.210
- Understand?
- Yes, ma'am!

00:48:30.420 --> 00:48:33.050
Damn it, l told them
we'd come to them!

00:48:33.050 --> 00:48:34.720
Cosmo knows...

00:48:34.720 --> 00:48:35.890
Watch it!

00:48:35.890 --> 00:48:38.470
Cosmo knows we're
down here, right?

00:48:38.470 --> 00:48:40.890
He's guiding the ship!

00:48:40.890 --> 00:48:45.730
Are more refugee children
from Frontier IV on that ship?

00:48:45.730 --> 00:48:47.320
Where are you from?

00:48:47.320 --> 00:48:48.730
Richmond.

00:48:48.730 --> 00:48:53.120
The Space Ark fled from there,
so they probably are.

00:48:54.450 --> 00:48:56.370
Okay, keep it coming!

00:48:56.370 --> 00:48:58.580
Park it right there!

00:48:58.580 --> 00:49:00.750
Gruce, it's combat-ready, right?

00:49:00.750 --> 00:49:01.960
That's the idea.

00:49:01.960 --> 00:49:03.830
Hey, it has a mouth!

00:49:03.830 --> 00:49:05.470
Close the mask!

00:49:06.270 --> 00:49:07.840
What?

00:49:07.840 --> 00:49:11.170
There used to be a mobile
suit with a face like this.

00:49:11.170 --> 00:49:12.340
Let me see...

00:49:12.510 --> 00:49:15.180
- See?
- Hey, right!

00:49:15.180 --> 00:49:17.260
It was called a "Gundam", right?

00:49:17.260 --> 00:49:21.270
Gruce, let's code-name
this thing "Gundam F91 ."

00:49:21.870 --> 00:49:23.770
Hey, where's this boy from?

00:49:23.770 --> 00:49:25.480
Seabook, you mean?

00:49:25.480 --> 00:49:27.940
Why's a kid from
that space boat here?

00:49:27.940 --> 00:49:29.440
What do you mean?

00:49:29.440 --> 00:49:31.900
Somebody has to do it, right?

00:49:31.900 --> 00:49:35.910
The SNRI F91 development
team in the colony...

00:49:35.910 --> 00:49:37.620
...ran away, right?

00:49:38.130 --> 00:49:42.250
He's Dr. Arno's son,
so maybe he can do it.

00:49:42.250 --> 00:49:44.500
What's my mother
have to do with it?

00:49:44.500 --> 00:49:47.840
Captain, report to
the bridge immediately!

00:49:48.940 --> 00:49:50.170
- Seabook!
- Yeah?

00:49:50.380 --> 00:49:52.380
You know the main switch?

00:49:52.380 --> 00:49:53.590
- Yeah.
- Do it.

00:49:53.840 --> 00:49:55.600
You got it!

00:49:57.940 --> 00:49:59.930
They got it working?

00:49:59.930 --> 00:50:02.350
Dwight, you'd better eat.
You too, Bertuo!

00:50:02.520 --> 00:50:03.730
Coming!

00:50:03.730 --> 00:50:05.600
You're having children help?

00:50:05.600 --> 00:50:07.350
Mrs. Elm, the medicine?

00:50:07.350 --> 00:50:09.060
We brought it with us.

00:50:09.060 --> 00:50:11.950
Didn't you manage
to get any mobile suits?

00:50:15.920 --> 00:50:17.570
This is a battlefield!

00:50:17.570 --> 00:50:18.450
Sorry!

00:50:18.660 --> 00:50:21.240
That's a resistance member?

00:50:21.410 --> 00:50:23.300
Why aren't there blueprints?

00:50:21.990 --> 00:50:22.990
No way!

00:50:22.990 --> 00:50:23.450
I work hard here!

00:50:23.450 --> 00:50:24.400
How should I know?

00:50:24.540 --> 00:50:24.830
So do I.

00:50:24.830 --> 00:50:26.250
On this ship, you do everything yourself

00:50:26.250 --> 00:50:27.080
Gimme.

00:50:27.620 --> 00:50:29.790
l wash the dishes, you know...

00:50:29.960 --> 00:50:31.170
Oh, she's still over there.

00:50:30.130 --> 00:50:31.170
l'll grab a bite.

00:50:31.170 --> 00:50:32.500
I think

00:50:31.210 --> 00:50:32.000
There's plenty.

00:50:32.500 --> 00:50:34.090
Thank you.

00:50:34.090 --> 00:50:35.660
Thanks.

00:50:35.660 --> 00:50:38.800
- What did she want?
- She's looking for Cecily.

00:50:38.800 --> 00:50:40.270
Cecily?

00:50:41.100 --> 00:50:44.310
Squad 4, assemble
on the upper deck!

00:50:44.310 --> 00:50:48.810
I could've sworn Cecily said
that her mother is missing...

00:50:48.810 --> 00:50:51.520
Enemy closing in.
Launch mobile suits!

00:50:51.520 --> 00:50:53.860
Don't let them get
close to the Space Ark!

00:50:54.030 --> 00:50:55.900
Noncombatants, take shelter!

00:50:56.070 --> 00:50:59.250
- Where are Reese and Kochun?
- ln the space boat.

00:51:01.280 --> 00:51:03.370
Are you here to get in the way?

00:51:03.370 --> 00:51:05.500
Birgit now launching!

00:51:06.950 --> 00:51:09.580
Don't let the enemy
get close to this vessel!

00:51:09.750 --> 00:51:11.630
Where's Birgit?

00:51:12.920 --> 00:51:14.550
Forget it!

00:51:14.550 --> 00:51:15.800
What?

00:51:15.800 --> 00:51:17.840
There are too
many people in here.

00:51:17.840 --> 00:51:19.470
Go out in the Gundam!

00:51:19.470 --> 00:51:21.720
And use the F91 as a decoy?

00:51:21.890 --> 00:51:25.720
Just use the coal heaps and
trees as cover and run, idiot!

00:51:25.720 --> 00:51:27.600
- Get going!
- Move it! l'll go!

00:51:27.600 --> 00:51:28.480
No way.

00:51:28.640 --> 00:51:30.060
Why not?

00:51:30.060 --> 00:51:33.310
lf you go, you'll end up like Arthur!

00:51:33.310 --> 00:51:34.480
I'll go.

00:51:34.480 --> 00:51:36.780
- Why?
- lt's like you've got a death wish!

00:51:36.980 --> 00:51:38.790
Look who's talking.

00:51:41.210 --> 00:51:43.910
lf I keep moving,
they won't get me...

00:51:43.910 --> 00:51:47.620
This is Seabook Arno in
the Gundam F91 moving out!

00:51:47.620 --> 00:51:50.210
Birgit, use #24! Launch!

00:51:53.330 --> 00:51:55.590
Can you get
the Gundam to stand?

00:51:55.590 --> 00:51:56.630
l hope so.

00:51:56.630 --> 00:51:58.310
Give it a shot!

00:52:00.400 --> 00:52:01.630
It's moving!

00:52:01.630 --> 00:52:02.680
lt's working, right?

00:52:02.680 --> 00:52:04.890
Just keep standing there!

00:52:04.890 --> 00:52:06.890
lt's working. lsn't that great?

00:52:06.890 --> 00:52:09.190
Yeah, and it's all thanks to you.

00:52:11.620 --> 00:52:14.730
With no pilot suit,
l won't be held in place...

00:52:14.730 --> 00:52:17.020
Take a gun! Grab the top one!

00:52:17.020 --> 00:52:18.480
Is it compatible?

00:52:18.650 --> 00:52:22.450
It was made for the F91 .
lt's already been calibrated!

00:52:22.610 --> 00:52:24.120
What're you doing?

00:52:24.120 --> 00:52:27.080
Once you're right in front of it,
just set it on auto!

00:52:27.080 --> 00:52:28.290
Seabook?

00:52:28.450 --> 00:52:31.500
- How long'll you make Birgit wait?
- Colonel Cosmo!

00:52:31.500 --> 00:52:34.470
I can't stand by and watch,
so l'm taking command!

00:52:38.190 --> 00:52:41.340
I can't believe Mom
built something like that...

00:52:41.340 --> 00:52:42.800
On the catapult!

00:52:42.800 --> 00:52:44.550
You can do it, Seabook!

00:52:44.550 --> 00:52:46.260
Seabook's in there?

00:52:46.260 --> 00:52:47.810
Okay!

00:52:48.450 --> 00:52:50.650
Stand by to launch the Gundam!

00:52:52.740 --> 00:52:55.020
- Engineering!
- Get us airborne!

00:52:55.020 --> 00:52:56.980
If we launch now, they'd see us!

00:52:56.980 --> 00:52:59.330
We'll be a target if we stay here!

00:53:09.220 --> 00:53:12.210
Taking this colony
would be child's play.

00:53:12.210 --> 00:53:15.710
Why do Father and
Grandfather hesitate?

00:53:15.710 --> 00:53:17.130
They're nothing!

00:53:26.690 --> 00:53:29.150
How many of 'em are there?

00:53:30.820 --> 00:53:34.280
There's a cruiser
hiding in the forest!

00:53:39.500 --> 00:53:40.910
Bastard!

00:53:42.460 --> 00:53:43.870
Here he comes!

00:53:51.800 --> 00:53:53.370
lt's going down...

00:53:53.370 --> 00:53:54.710
Where's Birgit?

00:53:58.630 --> 00:54:01.460
Can you handle the F91 ?

00:54:01.460 --> 00:54:02.810
l'm managing!

00:54:06.590 --> 00:54:08.390
l hit them...

00:54:10.400 --> 00:54:12.640
The pilots are dead...

00:54:13.120 --> 00:54:14.860
Are they dead?

00:54:19.290 --> 00:54:21.900
They couldn't have
had real firepower...

00:54:21.900 --> 00:54:25.490
...so how did I lose three
suits and have two damaged?

00:54:25.490 --> 00:54:28.120
"Pride goeth before the fall"?

00:54:29.220 --> 00:54:31.620
l couldn't believe it!

00:54:31.620 --> 00:54:34.040
l thought he was a simple baker!

00:54:34.040 --> 00:54:37.920
Theo's a traitor. He moved
close to the guest palace...

00:54:37.920 --> 00:54:40.840
...wagging his tail for the Ronahs.

00:54:40.840 --> 00:54:42.590
Hey, what about Cecily?

00:54:42.590 --> 00:54:44.720
That damn Ronah girl!

00:54:47.530 --> 00:54:49.260
"Ronah girl"?

00:54:49.260 --> 00:54:50.980
What's going on?

00:54:57.290 --> 00:54:58.730
Hurry it up.

00:54:58.730 --> 00:55:00.150
Almost done.

00:55:05.900 --> 00:55:07.950
l'll test the sensors!

00:55:07.950 --> 00:55:10.160
Hook up the cord!

00:55:10.160 --> 00:55:12.410
Hey, it's the plug down there!

00:55:12.410 --> 00:55:14.370
Got it.

00:55:14.370 --> 00:55:16.620
- Here goes!
- Okay!

00:55:16.620 --> 00:55:18.000
lt's working!

00:55:32.280 --> 00:55:34.400
I can't live alone...

00:55:34.990 --> 00:55:38.400
...but l can't work up
the nerve to commit suicide.

00:55:47.030 --> 00:55:49.450
Who's there? Guards!

00:55:49.450 --> 00:55:51.410
- l knew it was you, Cecily.
- Seabook...

00:55:51.410 --> 00:55:53.820
You're alive!

00:55:53.820 --> 00:55:57.190
Everybody's worried.
l came to get you.

00:55:57.190 --> 00:55:58.450
Where is he?

00:55:58.660 --> 00:55:59.870
- Come on!
- Why did you come now?

00:55:59.560 --> 00:56:00.280
Lady Berah's room!

00:56:00.330 --> 00:56:01.710
lt's already too late!

00:56:01.710 --> 00:56:02.960
Too late?

00:56:03.850 --> 00:56:05.430
It's too late!

00:56:14.740 --> 00:56:16.890
Who on Earth was that?

00:56:16.890 --> 00:56:18.480
You saved me.

00:56:19.030 --> 00:56:20.520
You cut your hair?

00:56:20.520 --> 00:56:21.860
Yes.

00:56:23.250 --> 00:56:25.270
Thank heavens you're safe.

00:56:25.270 --> 00:56:26.480
What happened to your hair?

00:56:26.650 --> 00:56:31.650
I decided I needed discipline to
be part of the Ronah family...

00:56:31.650 --> 00:56:33.490
...so l cut my hair.

00:56:33.490 --> 00:56:38.040
When it grows back, l'd like to be
the heir to Cosmo Babylonia.

00:56:38.040 --> 00:56:42.000
Oh, so that ruffian
interrupted your resolution.

00:56:42.000 --> 00:56:43.670
A burglar, perhaps.

00:56:43.670 --> 00:56:47.750
Due to this, I now see Federation
policies must be rectified.

00:56:47.750 --> 00:56:49.510
I see!

00:56:49.510 --> 00:56:52.180
You'll be the idol of our new era?

00:57:04.370 --> 00:57:05.900
Here they come!

00:57:06.060 --> 00:57:08.070
Cool! Den'an Zons!

00:57:08.070 --> 00:57:09.990
That's a Den'an Gei!

00:57:21.200 --> 00:57:23.040
A beam flag! Awesome!

00:57:23.210 --> 00:57:25.920
Well over 100 years into the UC...

00:57:25.920 --> 00:57:30.050
...Federation high officials
pollute the Earth once again...

00:57:30.050 --> 00:57:31.880
...destroying humanity's
one and only treasure!

00:57:31.880 --> 00:57:32.970
He's here.

00:57:32.970 --> 00:57:36.220
Knowing that changing the system is impossible...

00:57:33.010 --> 00:57:34.630
Can you catch him?

00:57:34.630 --> 00:57:35.720
We'll try.

00:57:35.720 --> 00:57:37.260
- Please do.
- Yes, ma'am.

00:57:36.220 --> 00:57:39.310
We decided to form Cosmo Babylonia

00:57:39.310 --> 00:57:42.560
The Crossbone Vanguard is its advance guard!

00:57:42.560 --> 00:57:47.650
You who were abandoned to dwell in this newly rebuilt colony...

00:57:47.650 --> 00:57:51.730
...must each use your talents to protect the entire Earth sphere!

00:57:51.730 --> 00:57:54.150
What? There's a sniper!

00:57:54.320 --> 00:57:58.990
To those who disagree with us,
l would say come kill me!

00:57:54.360 --> 00:57:56.950
It came from the south! What should we do?

00:57:58.990 --> 00:58:01.040
I will not run or hide!

00:58:01.200 --> 00:58:02.910
That's telling 'em, lron Mask!

00:58:02.910 --> 00:58:04.620
Down with the Federation!

00:58:04.620 --> 00:58:07.540
We don't pay taxes so that Fed suits can go down to Earth!

00:58:09.560 --> 00:58:13.210
Cecily, those who gain
power using military force...

00:58:13.210 --> 00:58:15.840
...maintain control through force.

00:58:15.840 --> 00:58:17.380
Why can't you see that?

00:58:17.550 --> 00:58:20.140
Saying reform has
started is crazy...

00:58:20.140 --> 00:58:21.180
...when nothing
has changed at all!

00:58:21.180 --> 00:58:22.010
Seabook?

00:58:23.640 --> 00:58:24.640
I found him!

00:58:24.640 --> 00:58:27.690
Change the world through
the Crossbone Vanguard!

00:58:27.850 --> 00:58:29.450
Move forward!

00:58:30.210 --> 00:58:33.610
Change the world through
the Crossbone Vanguard!

00:58:33.610 --> 00:58:34.990
Get in!

00:58:37.910 --> 00:58:39.210
Get outta here!

00:58:40.340 --> 00:58:44.590
Annamarie squadron, Georgia
Avenue in Block 5 ASAP.

00:58:45.470 --> 00:58:46.750
Gundam?

00:58:46.750 --> 00:58:48.170
It's a mobile suit?

00:58:48.170 --> 00:58:51.930
Yeah, it's nuts to run
resistance activities here.

00:59:06.930 --> 00:59:09.730
Just one unknown mobile suit?

00:59:09.730 --> 00:59:13.740
Have Annamarie track it and
find the resistance hideout.

00:59:14.500 --> 00:59:17.150
lt's better if it's their new suit!

00:59:17.150 --> 00:59:18.450
Roger!

00:59:23.880 --> 00:59:25.740
Reese is waiting for us.

00:59:25.740 --> 00:59:27.960
Hold on a little longer.

00:59:27.960 --> 00:59:29.860
l'm fine.

00:59:29.860 --> 00:59:33.430
l think you've got
Monica all wrong.

00:59:34.100 --> 00:59:36.340
You mean Mom? l don't think so.

00:59:36.510 --> 00:59:41.590
When she stopped breastfeeding
Reese, she was hysterical.

00:59:41.590 --> 00:59:46.650
l loved Monica,
but l loved her work, too.

00:59:47.320 --> 00:59:51.520
But she didn't go back to work
on a weapon like this, right?

00:59:51.520 --> 00:59:56.400
You can't develop bio-computers
on an individual level.

00:59:56.400 --> 01:00:00.900
But you hated seeing your alloy
research used by the military...

01:00:00.900 --> 01:00:03.740
...so you became a welder.

01:00:03.740 --> 01:00:05.660
Didn't it make you mad?

01:00:05.660 --> 01:00:09.590
I did a good job
raising you and Reese...

01:00:10.470 --> 01:00:12.790
l did a good job...

01:00:12.790 --> 01:00:14.080
Dad?

01:00:14.080 --> 01:00:16.970
Dad!

01:00:23.490 --> 01:00:26.470
When we finally
see each other again...

01:00:26.470 --> 01:00:28.930
...why's it have to be like this?

01:00:28.930 --> 01:00:31.280
Why, Dad?

01:00:34.290 --> 01:00:36.900
We're going to bury
him in space, Reese.

01:00:37.070 --> 01:00:39.360
No, l'll never leave him!

01:00:39.360 --> 01:00:40.900
Hey!

01:00:40.900 --> 01:00:42.740
Understand?

01:00:42.740 --> 01:00:45.700
This is what your ego got you!

01:00:45.700 --> 01:00:47.410
If you hadn't left alone...

01:00:47.410 --> 01:00:50.750
...'cause you can fly the Gundam,
your dad wouldn't be dead!

01:00:50.750 --> 01:00:56.420
Long ago, there were mobile
suit specialists called Newtypes.

01:00:56.420 --> 01:00:59.670
They were pretty much
miserable individuals.

01:00:59.670 --> 01:01:01.760
That's enough, Birgit!

01:01:01.760 --> 01:01:03.930
What should we do with him?

01:01:03.930 --> 01:01:05.430
Any ideas, Nanto?

01:01:05.430 --> 01:01:08.810
lf he were in the army,
this case would mean the brig.

01:01:08.810 --> 01:01:11.270
I don't know how
those guys'll handle it.

01:01:11.270 --> 01:01:12.940
He brought army regulars...

01:01:13.140 --> 01:01:14.980
So this is the Gundam?

01:01:14.980 --> 01:01:18.020
- Damn warmonger.
- Lt. Bardo of the 3rd Army?

01:01:18.020 --> 01:01:21.190
You can't say you're
an "acting" captain anymore.

01:01:21.190 --> 01:01:22.820
This may be a training ship...

01:01:22.820 --> 01:01:24.780
...but l want your help
against the Crossbone.

01:01:24.780 --> 01:01:27.280
We have no regular army members.

01:01:27.450 --> 01:01:29.790
This motley crew
you've gathered...

01:01:29.790 --> 01:01:33.710
...is far more effective
than paid soldiers.

01:01:33.540 --> 01:01:36.460
You're the one who
scouted in the Gundam?

01:01:37.330 --> 01:01:38.500
Uh, no...

01:01:38.500 --> 01:01:41.510
Oh, it was you?

01:01:41.510 --> 01:01:44.680
Colonel Cosmo,
he's an amateur!

01:01:44.680 --> 01:01:45.800
It's hopeless.

01:01:45.800 --> 01:01:49.720
The Crossbone is going
to kill everyone in this colony!

01:01:49.720 --> 01:01:54.020
l thought that stuff was just
rumors started by you guys!

01:01:54.020 --> 01:01:58.650
The Crossbone needs human
resources for Cosmo Babylonia.

01:01:58.650 --> 01:02:03.360
They'll purge the excess people
polluting the Earth and Moon.

01:02:03.360 --> 01:02:06.610
The colony's people
will be exterminated!

01:02:06.610 --> 01:02:07.700
With gas?

01:02:07.700 --> 01:02:11.620
Reports say they have
a machine that only kills humans.

01:02:14.250 --> 01:02:16.370
Is Cecily...

01:02:16.370 --> 01:02:18.040
Cecily...

01:02:18.040 --> 01:02:21.670
ls she going to help
them massacre everyone?

01:02:23.050 --> 01:02:25.010
No, she couldn't...

01:02:31.050 --> 01:02:34.640
Dad, what should l do?

01:02:54.790 --> 01:02:56.160
Name, please.

01:02:56.160 --> 01:02:58.170
Theo Fairchild.

01:03:04.800 --> 01:03:07.510
Is Carozzo in his office?

01:03:07.510 --> 01:03:09.260
He's in a war council.

01:03:09.260 --> 01:03:10.390
I see.

01:03:10.390 --> 01:03:12.350
We'll wait for him.

01:03:12.970 --> 01:03:15.560
Are you really going
to see him, Nadia?

01:03:15.560 --> 01:03:20.270
I left Cecily with you to fool
my father and ex-husband.

01:03:21.230 --> 01:03:22.860
l know that.

01:03:22.860 --> 01:03:24.940
l never told them.

01:03:24.940 --> 01:03:28.070
You have to understand
they found out on their own.

01:03:28.280 --> 01:03:29.820
Of course.

01:03:30.410 --> 01:03:34.030
It's not easy,
living near the Ronahs.

01:03:34.620 --> 01:03:36.370
It's Carozzo.

01:03:36.370 --> 01:03:38.210
Don't be overeager, Berah.

01:03:38.370 --> 01:03:39.670
- Yes.
- Berah?

01:03:39.670 --> 01:03:40.790
Cecily!

01:03:40.790 --> 01:03:42.630
Not now!

01:03:43.920 --> 01:03:46.260
Stand back. lt's Nadia.

01:03:46.420 --> 01:03:48.300
Cecily, let's go home.

01:03:48.300 --> 01:03:50.380
- Return to the ship.
- Yes, sir!

01:03:50.380 --> 01:03:54.300
Even if you are Carozzo,
l won't let you have this child.

01:03:54.300 --> 01:03:57.140
If you knew that
it was because of you...

01:03:57.140 --> 01:04:01.140
...that l had to wear this mask,
you wouldn't be able to say that.

01:04:01.140 --> 01:04:04.610
You're the aggressor here,
so stop playing the victim!

01:04:04.610 --> 01:04:08.820
Father, why did you let
him get away with this?

01:04:08.820 --> 01:04:12.990
A girl controlled by her emotions
who disregards her noble birth...

01:04:12.990 --> 01:04:14.910
...is no daughter of mine.

01:04:14.910 --> 01:04:18.370
Let Berah decide her own future.

01:04:18.370 --> 01:04:20.620
She's not old enough!

01:04:20.620 --> 01:04:24.750
Mother, we can discuss this
once the operation is concluded.

01:04:24.750 --> 01:04:27.460
Cecily, you're not Berah Ronah.

01:04:27.630 --> 01:04:32.260
No, l'm Berah Ronah,
pilot of the Vigna Ghina.

01:04:32.260 --> 01:04:34.180
The "freedom" you speak of...

01:04:34.180 --> 01:04:36.680
...sounds like an excuse
to shirk one's duties.

01:04:36.680 --> 01:04:39.100
- You're wrong!
- Nadia!

01:04:39.100 --> 01:04:41.940
When man followed his
passions like a beast...

01:04:41.940 --> 01:04:45.060
...he almost drained all
of the Earth sphere dry.

01:04:45.060 --> 01:04:46.360
Why can't you understand that?

01:04:47.650 --> 01:04:50.530
You never had the courage
to say that without that mask!

01:04:51.700 --> 01:04:54.780
l, too, am a man with emotions.

01:04:54.780 --> 01:04:58.700
lf it weren't for this mask, I may
have just beaten you to death.

01:04:58.700 --> 01:05:01.500
I wear this mask
to hold that in check.

01:05:01.500 --> 01:05:05.710
This is an era in which man
must restrain his passions.

01:05:05.710 --> 01:05:10.300
l would be happy if you were
to rest and reconcile with Father.

01:05:12.130 --> 01:05:13.590
Theo?

01:05:16.720 --> 01:05:18.470
Murderer!

01:05:19.180 --> 01:05:20.640
What?

01:05:30.070 --> 01:05:34.320
When you give the signal that
the three-pronged recon is done...

01:05:34.320 --> 01:05:35.820
...our mobile suits will launch.

01:05:35.820 --> 01:05:36.870
Yes, sir!

01:05:36.870 --> 01:05:38.080
- Let's go!
- Yes, ma'am!

01:05:38.080 --> 01:05:40.950
If we take control of
Frontier I on this mission...

01:05:40.950 --> 01:05:42.410
...we'll be able to have fun, right?

01:05:42.580 --> 01:05:46.080
We still have to mop up
on Earth, remember?

01:05:48.210 --> 01:05:50.340
Test it again!

01:05:50.340 --> 01:05:51.800
- I'll be right there.
- Yes, ma'am!

01:05:51.960 --> 01:05:53.920
- I leave it to you.
- Yes, sir!

01:05:53.920 --> 01:05:55.050
Lt. Zabine!

01:05:55.050 --> 01:05:56.470
Annamarie?

01:05:56.470 --> 01:05:58.800
There are more
enemies than expected.

01:05:58.800 --> 01:06:01.770
Be careful while out
on recon, all right?

01:06:01.770 --> 01:06:04.520
You should be careful,
since you'll be out first.

01:06:04.520 --> 01:06:07.560
Oh, wedge your
toes into the hatch.

01:06:07.560 --> 01:06:09.110
Thanks.

01:06:09.110 --> 01:06:12.070
You're coming too, Lady Berah?

01:06:12.070 --> 01:06:16.860
l may just get in the way,
but Zabine says he'll look after me.

01:06:17.530 --> 01:06:19.620
W-Well, be careful.

01:06:19.620 --> 01:06:21.580
l'll go on ahead.

01:06:21.580 --> 01:06:24.330
We're counting on you.

01:06:26.420 --> 01:06:28.250
lt's strange someone your rank...

01:06:28.250 --> 01:06:32.000
...doesn't know everything
about the Zamouth Garr.

01:06:32.000 --> 01:06:33.760
The captain doesn't either.

01:06:33.760 --> 01:06:34.920
That's the way it is.

01:06:35.130 --> 01:06:36.760
l see...

01:06:37.590 --> 01:06:41.100
It'll berth at the asteroid
end of Frontier I...

01:06:41.100 --> 01:06:42.640
...and be used as a beachhead.

01:06:42.640 --> 01:06:44.930
Is that all there is
to this operation?

01:06:45.180 --> 01:06:46.520
Miss?

01:06:46.520 --> 01:06:50.610
He may be my father,
but l can't trust Carozzo.

01:06:50.610 --> 01:06:53.730
I think he has something
else in mind.

01:06:53.730 --> 01:06:58.360
Gillet works under lron Mask,
so if you keep an eye on him...

01:06:58.360 --> 01:07:01.410
...you may find out what
the code "Bug" means.

01:07:02.120 --> 01:07:03.240
"Bug"?

01:07:03.240 --> 01:07:05.370
An example of how hard it is...

01:07:05.370 --> 01:07:07.620
...to know all of
our inner workings.

01:07:07.620 --> 01:07:10.250
Do you have something
against the Ronahs?

01:07:10.250 --> 01:07:13.630
l was involved in
the formation of the Crossbone.

01:07:13.630 --> 01:07:15.920
l know that Meitzer
and lron Mask...

01:07:15.920 --> 01:07:19.630
...don't mix personal
feelings and ideology.

01:07:20.430 --> 01:07:21.970
Neither do l.

01:07:22.640 --> 01:07:26.100
Annamarie's recon unit
ready for launch!

01:07:37.360 --> 01:07:38.820
This too?

01:07:38.820 --> 01:07:40.240
Thanks, Leah.

01:07:41.200 --> 01:07:44.580
Seabook said
he'd be right back...

01:07:44.580 --> 01:07:46.330
...so wait a little bit longer, okay?

01:07:46.580 --> 01:07:50.000
Well?
lf Cecily's joined the Ronahs...

01:07:50.000 --> 01:07:52.500
...she's putting in
a good word for us, right?

01:07:52.500 --> 01:07:53.500
Seabook!

01:07:53.500 --> 01:07:56.630
If we brought them the F91 ...

01:07:56.630 --> 01:07:59.800
...they'd probably make
us Babylonian citizens.

01:07:59.800 --> 01:08:03.140
But how can a soldier's son
think that way, Dwight?

01:08:03.140 --> 01:08:06.060
Dorothy, Sam, and Azuma
are with me on this.

01:08:06.060 --> 01:08:10.270
Even Acting Captain Leahlee
is thinking of getting out of here.

01:08:10.270 --> 01:08:14.150
You're just saying that because
you miss Cecily, aren't you?

01:08:14.150 --> 01:08:16.110
What's wrong with that?

01:08:16.780 --> 01:08:19.030
We're on battle alert!

01:08:19.030 --> 01:08:21.740
How about getting into
your pilot suit, Newtype?

01:08:21.740 --> 01:08:23.240
Who's a Newtype?

01:08:23.240 --> 01:08:24.830
You're gonna pilot it!

01:08:25.030 --> 01:08:28.580
Are you going to let your
sister and those kids die?

01:08:28.580 --> 01:08:30.830
You old bastard...

01:08:31.040 --> 01:08:32.670
Right a bit more!

01:08:32.670 --> 01:08:34.750
- Starboard, she said!
- I heard!

01:08:36.130 --> 01:08:39.170
That's our base?

01:08:39.170 --> 01:08:41.300
It's a bunch of rookies.

01:08:41.300 --> 01:08:44.590
Anyway, we made it
easier for 'em to land.

01:08:45.970 --> 01:08:48.180
Am l great or what?

01:08:48.180 --> 01:08:51.890
Now we don't have to worry
about being attacked from below.

01:08:51.890 --> 01:08:54.230
Yeah, we're on a coal heap.

01:08:54.230 --> 01:08:56.900
Cain, have Birgit and
Seabook sweep the area.

01:08:57.110 --> 01:08:59.780
To check out our
escape route, huh?

01:08:59.780 --> 01:09:01.780
- Acting Captain!
- Birgit!

01:09:01.780 --> 01:09:03.320
Clear the deck!

01:09:03.320 --> 01:09:05.030
We'll receive an enemy suit.

01:09:05.030 --> 01:09:05.870
We're on it!

01:09:06.030 --> 01:09:09.200
This is Birgit in #24!
l'm heading out!

01:09:10.000 --> 01:09:12.410
What a good pilot...

01:09:12.410 --> 01:09:17.040
I'd like our orders to come from
either the 3rd Army or the 35th.

01:09:17.040 --> 01:09:20.010
They have their hands
full guarding the outside.

01:09:20.010 --> 01:09:21.170
This is Seabook!

01:09:21.420 --> 01:09:24.090
Gundam F91 moving out!

01:09:24.090 --> 01:09:26.140
Don't lean too far into it!

01:09:31.980 --> 01:09:34.020
- Hey!
- ls that safe?

01:09:34.020 --> 01:09:36.060
What's he doing?

01:09:36.730 --> 01:09:38.900
Hey, a new model!

01:09:38.900 --> 01:09:41.280
Does that guy know
what he's doing?

01:09:44.530 --> 01:09:46.240
Seabook, are you okay?

01:09:46.240 --> 01:09:48.660
I faked about half of that.

01:09:48.660 --> 01:09:51.410
Didn't you say you
wanted to talk to me?

01:09:51.410 --> 01:09:55.710
I'll tell you this over a contact
circuit so we won't be overheard.

01:09:55.960 --> 01:09:56.960
Right.

01:09:56.960 --> 01:10:01.590
l'm going to the port to find an
escape route for the Space Ark.

01:10:01.590 --> 01:10:02.710
Oh, roger.

01:10:02.710 --> 01:10:05.470
Memorize the terrain
around the Space Ark.

01:10:05.470 --> 01:10:06.760
Yes, sir!

01:10:10.970 --> 01:10:15.140
I wonder if this bio-sensor
is syncing with my biorhythm?

01:10:15.690 --> 01:10:17.770
lt's Mom's, so l bet...

01:10:20.820 --> 01:10:22.230
What?

01:10:22.230 --> 01:10:24.110
l'll blast your ass! Move it!

01:10:28.320 --> 01:10:32.240
Being bigger and a paid
soldier makes you better?

01:10:34.700 --> 01:10:39.040
Once the Zamouth Garr berths
at Frontier l's mine section...

01:10:39.040 --> 01:10:41.920
...and the Bugs are activated,
this mission will be over.

01:10:42.170 --> 01:10:45.260
Yes, and if
the test is successful...

01:10:45.260 --> 01:10:47.590
...we destroy humanity
on the Earth and Moon?

01:10:47.800 --> 01:10:50.350
That's what
testing grounds are for.

01:10:50.350 --> 01:10:53.350
I remind you that
you're under strict orders...

01:10:53.350 --> 01:10:54.810
...not to harm the colony.

01:10:54.810 --> 01:10:58.140
Commencing decompression!
All pilots, board your craft!

01:10:58.140 --> 01:11:01.110
Zabine,
thanks for looking after me.

01:11:01.310 --> 01:11:02.730
Not at all.

01:11:02.730 --> 01:11:06.820
You say the Vigna Ghina is easier
to pilot than the Den'an class.

01:11:06.820 --> 01:11:10.160
It seems you truly are
a Newtype, Lady Berah.

01:11:11.160 --> 01:11:14.700
Don't flatter a novice into going
out by herself, all right?

01:11:14.910 --> 01:11:19.330
My Black Vanguard Squadron will
protect you from the perimeter.

01:11:19.330 --> 01:11:20.540
So then...

01:11:20.540 --> 01:11:22.880
All mobile suits, launch!

01:11:42.860 --> 01:11:45.570
The Dorel team will
ignore obstacles en route...

01:11:45.570 --> 01:11:47.400
...and go straight to the Stone.

01:11:47.400 --> 01:11:49.110
Follow my flag!

01:11:58.000 --> 01:11:59.250
l'll go first.

01:11:59.250 --> 01:12:00.960
Be my guest.

01:12:07.050 --> 01:12:08.800
I'm flying...

01:12:10.510 --> 01:12:12.090
The Chareux crest?

01:12:15.180 --> 01:12:17.930
She fell right into formation.

01:12:17.930 --> 01:12:21.810
I'm starting to believe that
a Newtype is someone...

01:12:21.810 --> 01:12:25.980
...who can grasp the essence
of something just by seeing it.

01:12:30.320 --> 01:12:34.370
lf l halt their reinforcements,
I won't lose to Zabine.

01:12:40.540 --> 01:12:43.460
lf she had defected
a week earlier...

01:12:43.460 --> 01:12:45.630
...the data would've
been easier to swap.

01:12:45.630 --> 01:12:47.250
- Is that it?
- Yeah.

01:12:47.250 --> 01:12:49.960
lt's Crossbone Vanguard data,
so it's accurate.

01:12:49.960 --> 01:12:53.680
Is Annamarie helping clean
up the altar Reese made?

01:12:53.680 --> 01:12:56.350
Yeah, the kids really like her.

01:12:56.350 --> 01:12:58.680
What's the deal
with all this paint?

01:13:01.980 --> 01:13:04.350
Is Annamarie
planning to go fight?

01:13:04.350 --> 01:13:06.060
Cosmic was ecstatic.

01:13:06.060 --> 01:13:08.190
- Thanks.
- Don't mention it.

01:13:08.190 --> 01:13:10.900
She's a high-ranking officer...

01:13:10.900 --> 01:13:13.320
Why'd she change sides?

01:13:13.490 --> 01:13:14.820
Sam! Azuma!

01:13:14.820 --> 01:13:15.620
Hurry it up!

01:13:15.870 --> 01:13:18.030
This is the last part!

01:13:18.030 --> 01:13:19.740
All hands, man your stations!

01:13:19.740 --> 01:13:22.550
- Run if you have to, okay?
- Yeah.

01:13:25.460 --> 01:13:28.210
The 38th is
deployed at Stone end.

01:13:28.210 --> 01:13:29.880
The Crossbone
are landing there.

01:13:30.090 --> 01:13:32.770
Decoy balloons, launch!

01:13:35.740 --> 01:13:39.100
3 minutes after the the barrage,
launch your mobile suits!

01:13:39.100 --> 01:13:40.310
Yes, sir!

01:13:40.310 --> 01:13:42.060
Receiving laser analysis.

01:13:42.060 --> 01:13:44.390
Enemy entering
secondary firing range, over!

01:13:44.390 --> 01:13:47.360
Don't let those pirates
have their way!

01:13:47.360 --> 01:13:49.900
All ships! Continuous barrage!

01:13:49.900 --> 01:13:51.700
Fire!

01:14:06.600 --> 01:14:08.880
We'll go north of their defenses.

01:14:08.880 --> 01:14:10.340
Keep going!

01:14:17.030 --> 01:14:18.800
lt's begun...

01:14:18.800 --> 01:14:20.190
Lady Berah.

01:14:20.700 --> 01:14:21.850
Yes?

01:14:21.850 --> 01:14:24.730
We'll finish the suits
the Dorel squadron misses.

01:14:24.730 --> 01:14:28.150
If any of our units lose
their nerve, chew them out.

01:14:28.350 --> 01:14:32.120
l'll watch you to see
how it's done, Zabine.

01:14:48.810 --> 01:14:50.960
Diversionary attack
on their ships!

01:14:50.960 --> 01:14:52.350
Fire!

01:14:58.490 --> 01:14:59.760
Sam and Azuma?

01:14:59.760 --> 01:15:03.390
They're worked up about using
the Space Ark's AA guns.

01:15:03.390 --> 01:15:04.430
Huh?

01:15:04.430 --> 01:15:06.570
Kochun's face is red.

01:15:09.370 --> 01:15:10.270
No!

01:15:10.520 --> 01:15:12.530
There's no air in there!

01:15:15.150 --> 01:15:17.400
- Idiot, you didn't need to close it!
- Ow!

01:15:17.400 --> 01:15:20.280
l didn't do it on purpose!

01:15:20.280 --> 01:15:22.370
Even Leah knows how
it's supposed to be done!

01:15:22.530 --> 01:15:25.090
Okay, ready...

01:15:26.810 --> 01:15:28.290
Find a seat, everybody!

01:15:28.290 --> 01:15:30.460
The Space Ark is moving?

01:15:30.460 --> 01:15:32.420
- Is it starting?
- Dwight?

01:15:32.420 --> 01:15:34.500
Aye, Acting Captain Leahlee!

01:15:34.500 --> 01:15:36.670
Once the mobile
suits are launched...

01:15:36.670 --> 01:15:40.010
...l want you kids to move
to the sunward port.

01:15:40.010 --> 01:15:43.350
The enemy's in the mine area,
so you can getaway.

01:15:43.350 --> 01:15:44.940
Okay, launch!

01:15:45.490 --> 01:15:47.560
Okay, clear out!

01:15:47.560 --> 01:15:51.230
Seabook, you and Annamarie
should stay on my wing.

01:15:51.230 --> 01:15:53.110
Can we fight inside the colony?

01:15:53.110 --> 01:15:55.280
l'll fight outside.

01:15:55.280 --> 01:15:56.990
Don't be stupid!

01:15:56.990 --> 01:16:00.320
They've busted through our
defenses on the mine end.

01:16:00.320 --> 01:16:01.530
Birgit!

01:16:01.530 --> 01:16:02.490
Yeah!

01:16:03.930 --> 01:16:07.450
This is Seabook in
the Gundam F91 moving out!

01:16:07.450 --> 01:16:09.170
All clear!

01:16:09.760 --> 01:16:14.170
So the Federation developed
a small, powerful mobile suit, too.

01:16:14.170 --> 01:16:16.430
Ready, Annamarie?

01:16:16.770 --> 01:16:20.930
We've detected the Crossbone's
advance guard inside the mine.

01:16:20.930 --> 01:16:22.640
l went up the ranks.

01:16:22.640 --> 01:16:24.720
I can't beat that Ronah woman.

01:16:24.720 --> 01:16:26.140
Say again?

01:16:26.140 --> 01:16:28.470
This is Annamarie. l'd like to go.

01:16:28.470 --> 01:16:31.190
lt'd be easier for us if she left.

01:16:31.190 --> 01:16:32.230
You think so?

01:16:32.230 --> 01:16:34.110
Annamarie, you can go.

01:16:34.110 --> 01:16:36.820
Thank you,
Acting Captain Leahlee.

01:16:41.750 --> 01:16:44.170
The F91 is flying again?

01:16:44.720 --> 01:16:48.540
But there shouldn't be any
spare parts here at SNRl...

01:16:49.790 --> 01:16:54.180
How can l see those
kids aboard the Space Ark?

01:16:56.980 --> 01:16:58.800
That's a space boat!

01:17:04.570 --> 01:17:07.180
l don't really think that woman...

01:17:07.180 --> 01:17:09.640
...who brought that data
would betray us.

01:17:09.640 --> 01:17:12.810
Seabook, I told you
not to fly past me!

01:17:12.810 --> 01:17:15.360
I can't let her go!

01:17:15.910 --> 01:17:17.490
The mine!

01:17:22.630 --> 01:17:25.320
Can Cosmo's ground
force advance more?

01:17:25.320 --> 01:17:28.920
Yeah, if they can't,
they'll take this area, too.

01:17:30.140 --> 01:17:33.340
The colony occupation
force is coming in.

01:17:41.150 --> 01:17:42.600
Stay put!

01:17:43.840 --> 01:17:45.390
What?

01:17:45.390 --> 01:17:47.600
Hey, what's happening?

01:17:47.600 --> 01:17:48.930
These guys are fast!

01:17:48.930 --> 01:17:51.350
A big Jegan type can't keep up!

01:17:51.350 --> 01:17:52.770
Really?

01:17:52.770 --> 01:17:54.070
Birgit!

01:18:02.090 --> 01:18:03.540
He's fast!

01:18:04.590 --> 01:18:06.870
A beam rifle won't do any good?

01:18:14.890 --> 01:18:17.470
This thing is just too powerful...

01:18:20.020 --> 01:18:21.920
Seabook, way to go!

01:18:21.920 --> 01:18:24.050
lt was just a fluke.

01:18:24.050 --> 01:18:26.340
It was firepower and mobility.

01:18:26.340 --> 01:18:28.720
I'll give 'em a diversion,
so you take 'em out!

01:18:28.720 --> 01:18:30.810
You can't be serious!

01:18:36.700 --> 01:18:38.320
Annamarie!

01:18:42.960 --> 01:18:45.450
- That was a Dahgi lris!
- Are you insane?

01:18:47.960 --> 01:18:51.580
Who'd fly into enemy
territory and then stop?

01:18:54.140 --> 01:18:56.160
Annamarie!

01:18:56.160 --> 01:18:58.420
There you are, Zabine!

01:19:05.320 --> 01:19:08.300
You have the gall to bring
that Ronah woman with you!

01:19:11.450 --> 01:19:14.140
Do you want that
family name so badly?

01:19:14.140 --> 01:19:17.440
The "friendly" ID signal it's
sending out had me fooled!

01:19:17.440 --> 01:19:21.690
Do you have to kill
me with a beam saber?

01:19:21.690 --> 01:19:23.360
Annamarie!

01:19:24.330 --> 01:19:26.320
You were my best trainee!

01:19:26.320 --> 01:19:28.120
Die with me!

01:19:30.420 --> 01:19:34.540
How can you justify
killing for a fake royal name?

01:19:38.060 --> 01:19:41.300
lf we die together,
will that end your resentment?

01:19:41.830 --> 01:19:43.970
Annamarie, get clear!

01:19:48.720 --> 01:19:51.300
l thought l taught
you that humans...

01:19:51.300 --> 01:19:54.220
...who can't deal with their
emotions are just trash.

01:19:55.200 --> 01:19:58.100
Zabine, what was that about?

01:19:58.100 --> 01:19:59.560
You saw what happened.

01:19:59.560 --> 01:20:02.560
A subordinate's betrayal
is my own shame.

01:20:02.560 --> 01:20:03.940
Forgive me.

01:20:03.940 --> 01:20:05.360
Really?

01:20:05.360 --> 01:20:06.900
Rear guard, move up!

01:20:06.900 --> 01:20:08.150
Zabine, the rear.

01:20:08.150 --> 01:20:10.250
No, Lady Berah!

01:20:11.920 --> 01:20:14.240
Bobulz, don't take
your eyes off her!

01:20:14.490 --> 01:20:15.880
Yes, sir!

01:20:17.500 --> 01:20:19.660
l don't sense Anna.

01:20:19.660 --> 01:20:20.960
Was she killed?

01:20:20.960 --> 01:20:22.300
Birgit!

01:20:25.670 --> 01:20:28.180
Don't put up a fight! Just go!

01:20:30.320 --> 01:20:31.760
I warned you!

01:20:40.080 --> 01:20:41.560
Seabook! Thanks!

01:20:41.560 --> 01:20:43.070
Here come more!

01:20:45.400 --> 01:20:48.330
Forget aiming,
just shoot forward!

01:20:51.670 --> 01:20:53.280
Got one!

01:20:58.550 --> 01:21:00.540
Let's do it! Three!

01:21:00.540 --> 01:21:01.880
Two!

01:21:03.420 --> 01:21:04.580
Fire!

01:21:07.250 --> 01:21:08.500
That's the way!

01:21:19.640 --> 01:21:21.520
Stop, don't give me more work!

01:21:24.810 --> 01:21:26.980
We managed
to make it through...

01:21:26.980 --> 01:21:28.480
An enemy?

01:21:28.480 --> 01:21:29.530
No...

01:21:29.530 --> 01:21:30.820
No, it's...

01:21:33.650 --> 01:21:35.700
Still three left dead ahead...

01:21:35.700 --> 01:21:37.330
The Space Ark?

01:21:43.250 --> 01:21:45.750
What the hell
are you doing here?

01:21:49.880 --> 01:21:53.380
You can't fire randomly
inside a colony!

01:22:01.810 --> 01:22:06.150
l can't believe they're using
mobile suits inside a colony...

01:22:09.270 --> 01:22:11.480
There's a cruiser
inside the colony?

01:22:11.480 --> 01:22:13.570
Where's Lady Berah?

01:22:13.570 --> 01:22:16.320
Bridge, main cannon
beam is too tight!

01:22:16.320 --> 01:22:17.660
Hit! Hit!

01:22:18.820 --> 01:22:20.280
He got away!

01:22:20.280 --> 01:22:23.450
- Come about 1 80 degrees!
- l'm on it!

01:22:24.080 --> 01:22:27.250
Cain, order Birgit
and Seabook to retreat!

01:22:27.460 --> 01:22:28.880
Roger!

01:22:36.300 --> 01:22:38.050
You can leave now!

01:22:38.050 --> 01:22:39.510
Get out!

01:22:39.510 --> 01:22:41.260
Another one?

01:22:45.270 --> 01:22:46.560
lt's fast!

01:22:51.570 --> 01:22:53.360
This type isn't in my database...

01:22:59.530 --> 01:23:01.200
Damn!

01:23:07.420 --> 01:23:10.250
You came in too far ahead!

01:23:10.250 --> 01:23:13.050
My gun's overheated!

01:23:22.640 --> 01:23:24.220
Lady Berah!

01:23:30.860 --> 01:23:32.270
Got him...

01:23:41.120 --> 01:23:44.080
l know that voice.
ls that you, Seabook?

01:23:44.580 --> 01:23:45.910
Seabook...

01:23:45.910 --> 01:23:46.870
Seabook!

01:23:46.870 --> 01:23:48.710
Cecily?

01:23:48.710 --> 01:23:49.790
Cecily!

01:23:49.790 --> 01:23:51.460
l hear you over the circuit.

01:23:51.460 --> 01:23:54.670
Is that really you
in there, Seabook?

01:23:54.670 --> 01:23:58.590
That's you in that
white suit, Cecily?

01:23:58.590 --> 01:24:00.130
But why?

01:24:01.340 --> 01:24:02.550
Cecily!

01:24:02.550 --> 01:24:04.180
It just happened.

01:24:04.180 --> 01:24:06.270
lt just worked out this way.

01:24:06.270 --> 01:24:07.430
What should l do?

01:24:07.430 --> 01:24:09.390
What do you mean?

01:24:09.390 --> 01:24:13.230
I thought you cut your hair
to go back to the Ronahs!

01:24:13.230 --> 01:24:14.230
No.

01:24:14.230 --> 01:24:18.490
You guys weren't around,
so I didn't think l had a choice!

01:24:18.490 --> 01:24:20.860
Really? That's what happened?

01:24:20.860 --> 01:24:24.030
l'm still Cecily Fairchild!

01:24:28.080 --> 01:24:31.040
Another mobile suit
type l've never seen.

01:24:32.630 --> 01:24:36.090
I admit that
l chose to accept it...

01:24:36.090 --> 01:24:38.960
...but l couldn't live
in that family anymore.

01:24:38.960 --> 01:24:40.510
They're the ones
who started this!

01:24:40.510 --> 01:24:43.800
They caused a massacre
on Frontier lV!

01:24:43.800 --> 01:24:45.470
l thought that was you!

01:24:45.470 --> 01:24:47.970
This ship's crew was killed...

01:24:47.970 --> 01:24:50.600
...and we've got amateurs
running a warship!

01:24:50.600 --> 01:24:54.270
Grandfather wanted to fix
that kind of system.

01:24:55.270 --> 01:24:57.900
There's no point
in arguing, Cecily.

01:24:58.530 --> 01:25:00.150
We were all dragged in.

01:25:00.150 --> 01:25:01.950
And l killed plenty of them.

01:25:01.950 --> 01:25:02.990
lt evens out.

01:25:02.990 --> 01:25:04.820
You're joking!

01:25:04.820 --> 01:25:07.120
lf the Crossbone
has Newtypes, too...

01:25:07.120 --> 01:25:08.870
...we have to take them out!

01:25:08.870 --> 01:25:10.120
Birgit.

01:25:10.120 --> 01:25:11.710
Captain!

01:25:11.710 --> 01:25:16.170
I get the impression that
your life is rather complicated.

01:25:16.170 --> 01:25:19.960
But I think l've seen
what our real enemy is.

01:25:19.960 --> 01:25:21.130
Really?

01:25:21.130 --> 01:25:25.180
Gruce, is her mobile suit usable?

01:25:25.180 --> 01:25:28.600
lt's the rattling in
the Gundam that worries me!

01:25:28.600 --> 01:25:31.060
We only need
to find a cockpit cover!

01:25:31.060 --> 01:25:33.520
Rush repairs on all suits!

01:25:33.520 --> 01:25:36.610
What do you have
in mind, Captain?

01:25:36.610 --> 01:25:39.070
We've made it
this far on blind luck.

01:25:39.070 --> 01:25:42.740
But we can't count on
any more luck, can we?

01:25:42.740 --> 01:25:46.160
We have to use everything
we can to get out of this.

01:25:46.160 --> 01:25:47.780
You have a point, but...

01:25:47.780 --> 01:25:51.330
I wonder how the battle's
going outside the sunward end?

01:25:51.330 --> 01:25:53.290
You're right...

01:25:53.290 --> 01:25:55.540
You can park
the space boat here!

01:25:55.540 --> 01:25:56.580
Nanto!

01:25:56.580 --> 01:25:58.210
Aye! l'll moor it!

01:25:58.210 --> 01:26:00.050
It's all yours.

01:26:00.050 --> 01:26:04.760
This isn't a military vessel,
so you can stay here.

01:26:04.760 --> 01:26:06.090
Thanks.

01:26:08.050 --> 01:26:10.600
The first one up front! Up front!

01:26:15.730 --> 01:26:16.810
Cecily?

01:26:16.810 --> 01:26:18.150
What's wrong?

01:26:21.070 --> 01:26:22.690
l...

01:26:30.200 --> 01:26:31.830
It's all right.

01:26:31.830 --> 01:26:34.540
You can stay here, okay?

01:26:36.920 --> 01:26:40.380
- l'm scared!
- Someone stop that boy!

01:26:42.090 --> 01:26:43.920
- Open it!
- Yes, sir!

01:26:43.920 --> 01:26:44.970
Thanks.

01:26:44.970 --> 01:26:46.130
Nobody else!

01:26:46.130 --> 01:26:47.470
Let go of her!

01:26:47.470 --> 01:26:49.930
Why can't we come in?

01:26:51.140 --> 01:26:54.180
l thought all the SNRI
staff fled to the Moon.

01:26:54.180 --> 01:26:56.690
We have orders
to evacuate, too.

01:26:56.690 --> 01:26:59.650
- The F91 was fighting here.
- l wouldn't know.

01:26:59.650 --> 01:27:02.690
The Space Ark
is here in this port.

01:27:02.690 --> 01:27:04.490
This area is locked down!

01:27:04.490 --> 01:27:05.860
Please.

01:27:05.860 --> 01:27:07.400
A-All right, be careful.

01:27:07.400 --> 01:27:09.910
Just use all parts of the boat!

01:27:09.910 --> 01:27:11.950
l heard
the Black Squadron's gone.

01:27:11.950 --> 01:27:14.790
Rumors are rumors.
Don't spread it.

01:27:14.790 --> 01:27:17.290
I think it's true.
Even Zabine was killed!

01:27:17.290 --> 01:27:19.420
Serves that lowborn right.

01:27:19.420 --> 01:27:21.590
They say one enemy suit did it.

01:27:21.590 --> 01:27:23.500
lt's our chance
to prove ourselves.

01:27:23.500 --> 01:27:28.130
- Won't they take this plant back?
- How's it coming?

01:27:28.130 --> 01:27:29.890
Powering the Zamouth Garr!

01:27:29.890 --> 01:27:32.390
Can't they trust us
to guard the place?

01:27:35.430 --> 01:27:39.140
lt's old, but I know why this
fusion reactor is necessary...

01:27:39.310 --> 01:27:42.400
...to acquire a vast amount
of power in a short time.

01:27:42.400 --> 01:27:45.820
But why does
the Zamouth Garr need this?

01:27:45.820 --> 01:27:50.410
The only connection l can
think of is the "Bug" code name.

01:27:59.710 --> 01:28:01.540
This is Zabine Chareux.

01:28:01.540 --> 01:28:03.880
Your catapult deck is sealed off.

01:28:03.880 --> 01:28:06.300
What about repairs
and resupply?

01:28:06.300 --> 01:28:08.800
This vessel has
a special mission...

01:28:08.800 --> 01:28:10.930
...under Iron Mask's
direct command.

01:28:10.930 --> 01:28:14.100
Have another ship handle
your repairs and resupply.

01:28:14.100 --> 01:28:17.100
All mobile suits are
to finish surviving units...

01:28:17.100 --> 01:28:18.810
...and protect the Zamouth Garr.

01:28:18.810 --> 01:28:20.100
Yes, sir!

01:28:22.100 --> 01:28:24.940
Berah's Vigna Ghina
isn't here, either?

01:28:24.940 --> 01:28:28.530
If she died in battle,
the old man won't complain.

01:28:28.530 --> 01:28:30.860
Gillet, can sunward
side operations...

01:28:31.070 --> 01:28:33.530
...be finished before
the Bugs are activated?

01:28:33.530 --> 01:28:36.160
Yes, that won't be a problem.

01:28:37.700 --> 01:28:41.580
We must ease the world's
burden, if only a little at a time.

01:28:45.130 --> 01:28:47.460
l appreciate all
you've done, Reese.

01:28:47.460 --> 01:28:48.800
Thank you.

01:28:49.300 --> 01:28:50.760
Reese?

01:28:52.180 --> 01:28:56.220
If you were in the colony,
why didn't you come sooner?

01:28:56.220 --> 01:29:00.850
I came back after l got on a ship
heading for the Moon, didn't l?

01:29:00.850 --> 01:29:02.640
l feel sorry for Dad.

01:29:02.640 --> 01:29:07.440
No, l guess he wasn't alone.
Seabook brought him back.

01:29:07.440 --> 01:29:09.030
I'm very sorry.

01:29:09.030 --> 01:29:13.820
Your father gave me his
blessing to go back to work!

01:29:13.820 --> 01:29:16.120
No, that's not why.

01:29:16.120 --> 01:29:19.080
I went back because
I loved my work.

01:29:20.540 --> 01:29:23.080
l'm sorry.

01:29:23.080 --> 01:29:24.500
Don't touch me!

01:29:24.500 --> 01:29:29.050
Seabook almost got killed
because you built that Gundam!

01:29:29.050 --> 01:29:30.550
What do you mean?

01:29:30.550 --> 01:29:32.880
Your son may be a Newtype.

01:29:32.880 --> 01:29:34.760
He's very perceptive.

01:29:34.760 --> 01:29:36.220
He is?

01:29:36.220 --> 01:29:39.680
Yes, he's already
distinguished himself in battle.

01:29:39.680 --> 01:29:41.730
He's fighting a war.

01:29:41.730 --> 01:29:43.480
Even the Gundam's shaken.

01:29:43.480 --> 01:29:44.690
W-Where is he?

01:29:44.690 --> 01:29:45.730
He's resting now.

01:29:45.730 --> 01:29:49.070
He's sleeping like he's dead.
l feel so sorry for him.

01:29:49.530 --> 01:29:51.740
We need every edge.

01:29:51.740 --> 01:29:55.950
Just helping with the control
systems check would be great.

01:29:55.950 --> 01:29:58.410
My own son using a weapon...

01:29:58.410 --> 01:30:02.750
That's not why
l helped develop the F91 !

01:30:02.750 --> 01:30:04.790
Why then, ma'am?

01:30:04.790 --> 01:30:09.130
You don't care who fights and
dies as long as it isn't your son?

01:30:09.710 --> 01:30:12.460
N-No, that's not what I meant.

01:30:12.460 --> 01:30:14.130
It's not!

01:30:14.130 --> 01:30:17.260
Everyone just wants
to escape this crazy war.

01:30:17.260 --> 01:30:19.930
But they're afraid
to leave here, too.

01:30:19.930 --> 01:30:24.020
What do you want me
to do about it, Reese?

01:30:24.020 --> 01:30:25.440
Tell me.

01:30:25.980 --> 01:30:29.480
Wars are scary and horrible,
and shouldn't be fought.

01:30:29.480 --> 01:30:34.400
Yes, that's why I was using
bio-computers to do good things.

01:30:34.650 --> 01:30:36.070
Mom.

01:30:36.070 --> 01:30:38.070
Forget the adult reasoning.

01:30:38.070 --> 01:30:40.910
Repairing the mobile suits
is what's important.

01:30:40.910 --> 01:30:43.250
If we don't get
that done, we'll all die.

01:30:43.250 --> 01:30:44.960
Seabook...

01:30:45.460 --> 01:30:48.750
Aren't we all grown up?
Both me and Reese?

01:30:51.040 --> 01:30:55.050
Let's think about why Cecily
and l are piloting mobile suits...

01:30:55.050 --> 01:30:58.390
...after the war's over, okay?

01:30:58.390 --> 01:31:01.760
But some theories say
Newtypes are evolved humans...

01:31:01.760 --> 01:31:04.770
...and that they can
eliminate war, right?

01:31:04.770 --> 01:31:07.940
If that's true, we ought
to try to find a way...

01:31:07.940 --> 01:31:12.820
...to change all humanity
into Newtypes, starting with us.

01:31:13.440 --> 01:31:16.900
Yes, but we have to survive first.

01:31:16.900 --> 01:31:21.370
It's tough to rethink things
and start over once you're dead.

01:31:21.370 --> 01:31:22.620
Dad...

01:31:22.620 --> 01:31:23.950
I understand.

01:31:23.950 --> 01:31:26.330
I'll do your father's share, too.

01:31:26.330 --> 01:31:28.170
Thanks, Mom.

01:31:30.170 --> 01:31:32.290
l'm proud of you, Seabook.

01:31:33.380 --> 01:31:34.840
You too, Reese.

01:31:52.610 --> 01:31:55.190
The battle's moved pretty far off.

01:31:55.190 --> 01:31:57.570
If we go for
the Moon right away...

01:31:57.570 --> 01:31:58.950
We'll be okay!

01:32:04.910 --> 01:32:06.870
Don't open that hatch!

01:32:06.870 --> 01:32:09.790
We're in the way,
clogging the corridor!

01:32:09.790 --> 01:32:12.170
The gun turret
is open to space!

01:32:12.170 --> 01:32:15.710
Move to the gun room
or to the center of the ship!

01:32:15.710 --> 01:32:19.170
- Which hatch should we use?
- That hatch goes to the center!

01:32:19.170 --> 01:32:20.340
We have kids!

01:32:20.340 --> 01:32:23.850
- You can't come in here.
- lt's dangerous in here!

01:32:23.850 --> 01:32:25.510
Why'd you let civilians aboard?

01:32:25.510 --> 01:32:26.770
We were busy.

01:32:26.770 --> 01:32:29.230
When I found out, it was too late.

01:32:29.560 --> 01:32:34.360
It'd be easy to have a mobile suit
paint a red cross on the ship.

01:32:34.360 --> 01:32:35.520
Yeah!

01:32:35.520 --> 01:32:36.980
And afterwards?

01:32:36.980 --> 01:32:39.900
We'd ditch it after
the cross is done!

01:32:39.900 --> 01:32:43.160
Are we really
a refugee or a hospital ship?

01:32:43.160 --> 01:32:45.450
I don't think that'll work now.

01:32:45.450 --> 01:32:49.580
Fighting is starting up
again inside Frontier I.

01:32:49.580 --> 01:32:50.540
And there?

01:32:50.540 --> 01:32:53.460
They say Cosmo's unit
has been wiped out!

01:32:53.460 --> 01:32:54.590
ls that true?

01:32:54.590 --> 01:32:56.420
I'll patch it through to you!

01:32:56.420 --> 01:32:59.090
l've never seen anything like it!
We need backup!

01:32:59.090 --> 01:33:00.920
Now setting course for the Moon.

01:33:01.800 --> 01:33:05.300
Mobile suits on standby
even after escape trajectory!

01:33:05.300 --> 01:33:08.180
Maintain Minovsky particle
density at combat levels!

01:33:11.770 --> 01:33:13.730
What are you doing?

01:33:13.730 --> 01:33:15.900
There's no need for you to go.

01:33:15.900 --> 01:33:18.780
Doing that won't make
us trust you any sooner.

01:33:18.780 --> 01:33:21.280
l understand that.

01:33:21.280 --> 01:33:27.450
But my Vigna Ghina's still sending
a Crossbone "friendly" lD code...

01:33:27.450 --> 01:33:30.410
...so l should be
able to help you two.

01:33:30.410 --> 01:33:33.250
And if the Feds
start shooting at you?

01:33:33.250 --> 01:33:35.710
Then l'll be the only casualty.

01:33:35.710 --> 01:33:37.040
Cecily.

01:33:37.920 --> 01:33:42.720
I was happy that the people
on this ship took me in...

01:33:42.720 --> 01:33:44.550
...without saying a word.

01:33:50.680 --> 01:33:53.140
- I'm counting on you, Birgit.
- For what?

01:33:53.140 --> 01:33:54.140
Seabook...

01:33:54.140 --> 01:33:56.560
She's trying to get herself killed.

01:33:56.560 --> 01:33:57.810
Who cares?

01:33:57.810 --> 01:34:01.230
That girl could've
been the Crossbone queen.

01:34:04.360 --> 01:34:06.660
l heard you, Mom.

01:34:09.280 --> 01:34:13.830
That's the first time l've seen you
worried about someone like that.

01:34:13.830 --> 01:34:15.620
ls it?

01:34:15.620 --> 01:34:17.210
She's a fine girl.

01:34:17.210 --> 01:34:18.920
l know.

01:34:27.550 --> 01:34:29.300
Deployment was flawless.

01:34:29.300 --> 01:34:30.930
If they breed as planned...

01:34:30.930 --> 01:34:35.560
...Frontier l's population
of 3 million will be gone in 2 or 3 days.

01:34:35.560 --> 01:34:37.480
If this test goes well...

01:34:37.480 --> 01:34:40.690
...drop the Bugs on
the Earth and Moon right away.

01:34:40.690 --> 01:34:44.530
This is a fine plan.
No one's conscience will be hurt.

01:34:44.530 --> 01:34:46.990
It's just a random
purging by machines.

01:35:04.510 --> 01:35:06.970
Damn bunch of tops!

01:35:12.430 --> 01:35:14.850
ls the colony breaking apart?

01:35:28.410 --> 01:35:30.620
They're not mobile suits...

01:35:30.620 --> 01:35:32.080
What are they?

01:35:32.780 --> 01:35:35.540
I have no idea. l'm sorry.

01:35:37.120 --> 01:35:38.870
Use her as a shield.

01:35:38.870 --> 01:35:40.420
Huh?

01:35:59.940 --> 01:36:01.230
Birgit!

01:36:02.810 --> 01:36:04.780
These are the Bugs?

01:36:06.650 --> 01:36:08.990
- What kind of machines?
- l don't know!

01:36:09.240 --> 01:36:11.660
The Crossbone Vanguard
had lots of factions.

01:36:11.660 --> 01:36:14.990
If vicious weapons like these
were used on the Earth...

01:36:17.700 --> 01:36:20.120
Wait, you think
you can beat them?

01:36:20.120 --> 01:36:22.750
Did Grandfather
have those things built?

01:36:36.430 --> 01:36:38.230
Birgit, don't be stupid!

01:36:46.530 --> 01:36:48.820
These things
only target humans?

01:36:55.280 --> 01:36:57.620
lt'll take more than that!

01:37:02.330 --> 01:37:04.080
You've got to move more!

01:37:06.290 --> 01:37:08.920
Damn... stupid... piece of...

01:37:10.470 --> 01:37:12.090
Get out of there!

01:37:24.400 --> 01:37:26.400
Birgit...

01:37:29.570 --> 01:37:30.990
These things...

01:37:30.990 --> 01:37:33.860
They're using them
to massacre everyone here.

01:37:33.860 --> 01:37:37.200
The Crossbone fleet
mobile suits were decoys!

01:37:37.200 --> 01:37:40.540
Nobody knows! Not Grandfather,
not the fleet, and not Zabine!

01:37:40.540 --> 01:37:42.210
- Meaning?
- lt's lron Mask!

01:37:42.210 --> 01:37:43.500
One man?

01:37:43.500 --> 01:37:46.460
- Yes!
- Then we have to kill him!

01:37:47.710 --> 01:37:50.840
But there are so many Bugs.
What should we do?

01:37:51.920 --> 01:37:53.010
lt's too dangerous!

01:37:53.010 --> 01:37:54.680
But it's the only way...

01:38:11.780 --> 01:38:13.320
Behind me?

01:38:21.580 --> 01:38:24.410
More! l need more
to come after me!

01:39:03.870 --> 01:39:06.750
That looks like the bow
of the Zamouth Garr...

01:39:48.040 --> 01:39:49.830
Was that a nuke?

01:39:50.540 --> 01:39:52.790
Did she do it?

01:39:52.790 --> 01:39:54.550
The Garr Prow was destroyed!

01:39:54.550 --> 01:39:56.340
l know. Find out how.

01:39:56.340 --> 01:39:58.380
No, l'll investigate.

01:39:58.380 --> 01:40:01.300
- Sir?
- This is a family matter.

01:40:01.850 --> 01:40:03.930
He's going out in the Rafflesia?

01:40:07.640 --> 01:40:11.020
Wait, was that
really the Zamouth Garr?

01:40:11.020 --> 01:40:13.980
- Berah sniped it.
- lt was her, all right.

01:40:13.980 --> 01:40:17.900
l'm picking up a new "friendly"
lD signal towards the Moon.

01:40:18.740 --> 01:40:20.030
ls that it?

01:40:20.030 --> 01:40:22.030
The color says it's a friendly...

01:40:22.030 --> 01:40:24.700
I've never seen
a code like this before...

01:40:24.700 --> 01:40:27.250
...but it's registered
in the computer.

01:40:27.250 --> 01:40:28.200
A Bug?

01:40:28.200 --> 01:40:29.500
lron Mask!

01:40:29.500 --> 01:40:31.750
- l'll challenge Berah.
- What?

01:40:31.750 --> 01:40:33.540
lt's acting strangely.

01:40:33.540 --> 01:40:35.460
lf we don't do something...

01:40:37.630 --> 01:40:41.010
A new Federation model?
lt's possible.

01:40:41.010 --> 01:40:44.350
This happened because the old
man doted on Berah too much.

01:40:44.970 --> 01:40:48.640
l misjudged. Lady Berah's
turned against us!

01:40:48.640 --> 01:40:49.980
Yes, sir!

01:40:57.190 --> 01:41:00.070
Don't let a single
mobile suit escape.

01:41:00.070 --> 01:41:02.030
Give a good accounting
of yourselves!

01:41:09.040 --> 01:41:11.660
3rd Army unable
to complete objective!

01:41:17.460 --> 01:41:21.930
Federation reinforcements from
the Moon detected dead ahead.

01:41:34.350 --> 01:41:35.650
What?

01:41:35.650 --> 01:41:37.230
Our carrier was hit!

01:41:37.230 --> 01:41:39.610
Is there an enemy
fleet back there?

01:41:41.990 --> 01:41:44.160
Here it comes! What is it?

01:41:51.160 --> 01:41:53.460
You're not alone, Berah?

01:41:57.500 --> 01:42:00.630
A man who can't do
anything without his mask...

01:42:00.630 --> 01:42:02.090
...says he'll change the world.

01:42:02.090 --> 01:42:05.300
Anyone who can
plan this is dangerous.

01:42:05.300 --> 01:42:07.510
Yes, he's the
real enemy, all right.

01:42:07.510 --> 01:42:10.680
Looks like the reinforcements
from the Moon are gone.

01:42:10.680 --> 01:42:13.140
I wish somebody
could call this off, but...

01:42:13.140 --> 01:42:17.310
We'll have to kill him, won't we?

01:42:17.310 --> 01:42:18.520
Looks that way.

01:42:18.520 --> 01:42:19.860
What's that light?

01:42:19.860 --> 01:42:24.950
lt feels like some evil spirit that's
throwing the universe into chaos.

01:42:28.030 --> 01:42:31.240
That was the F91
and the Vigna, wasn't it?

01:42:31.410 --> 01:42:34.410
The Space Ark's
telescopes confirm it.

01:42:34.410 --> 01:42:36.750
My brother is still fighting?

01:42:36.960 --> 01:42:40.340
He's trying to secure
an escape route for us.

01:42:40.340 --> 01:42:42.210
Fighting still in the upper right?

01:42:42.420 --> 01:42:44.050
Yes, ma'am!

01:42:44.050 --> 01:42:46.260
We can act as a refugee ship.

01:42:46.260 --> 01:42:48.090
Nice work, Dr. Arno.

01:42:48.090 --> 01:42:50.760
Of course.
They could only see two?

01:42:50.760 --> 01:42:53.310
Yes, no response from Birgit.

01:42:53.310 --> 01:42:54.980
l see...

01:42:54.980 --> 01:42:59.520
The F91 and the Vigna's flight
capabilities seem above average.

01:42:59.520 --> 01:43:01.980
Sorry, that's a
mother's foolish pride.

01:43:01.980 --> 01:43:07.320
No, I have to agree after seeing
him in action inside Frontier l.

01:43:07.320 --> 01:43:11.030
Seabook is showing us the way.

01:43:11.030 --> 01:43:13.240
Both him and the Gundam...

01:43:14.500 --> 01:43:16.920
Thank you, Captain.

01:43:23.300 --> 01:43:24.800
Here it comes!

01:43:29.470 --> 01:43:31.260
Don't, Cecily!

01:43:34.680 --> 01:43:36.480
ls that a Bug, too?

01:43:42.900 --> 01:43:45.070
Getaway, Cecily!

01:43:50.570 --> 01:43:54.490
Cecily, use the colony
wreckage as a shield!

01:43:57.500 --> 01:43:59.920
- Cecily, get back!
- But that's...

01:43:59.920 --> 01:44:01.330
Let me handle it!

01:44:10.590 --> 01:44:12.180
Here it comes!

01:44:14.720 --> 01:44:17.640
l'll cut these family ties myself!

01:44:23.310 --> 01:44:24.900
This one is fast.

01:44:24.900 --> 01:44:26.690
ls it a Newtype?

01:44:28.820 --> 01:44:31.070
Is that the cockpit?

01:44:33.320 --> 01:44:34.700
l knew it!

01:44:36.490 --> 01:44:38.500
l'll kill you myself!

01:44:52.760 --> 01:44:56.470
Gillet, l saw that thing
leave from this ship!

01:44:56.470 --> 01:44:57.680
What is it?

01:44:57.680 --> 01:44:59.600
You must mean the Rafflesia.

01:44:59.600 --> 01:45:01.520
But it doesn't concern me.

01:45:01.520 --> 01:45:03.310
What?

01:45:03.310 --> 01:45:05.730
Is this how Iron Mask operates?

01:45:05.730 --> 01:45:08.650
As I said,
it doesn't concern me.

01:45:12.320 --> 01:45:13.700
Cecily!

01:45:15.620 --> 01:45:17.950
I don't have the authority.

01:45:17.950 --> 01:45:20.460
But those who work
under lron Mask...

01:45:20.460 --> 01:45:23.500
...aren't the only ones
who can act as they see fit.

01:45:23.500 --> 01:45:25.500
Zabine!

01:45:25.500 --> 01:45:30.170
lf I didn't know about the Rafflesia,
then neither did Meitzer.

01:45:36.050 --> 01:45:39.720
The Zamouth Garr will stay
on standby till Iron Mask returns!

01:45:39.720 --> 01:45:41.560
- Understood?
- Yes, sir!

01:45:51.860 --> 01:45:53.700
You're in too close!

01:45:55.450 --> 01:45:57.620
Just a man-made thing...

01:46:04.620 --> 01:46:05.830
lron Mask!

01:46:05.830 --> 01:46:08.840
You want to be close,
so let's do it like this.

01:46:08.840 --> 01:46:10.920
You've been naughty.

01:46:10.920 --> 01:46:13.930
Children shouldn't
suspect what adults do.

01:46:13.930 --> 01:46:17.220
You're just rebelling
against Grandfather...

01:46:17.220 --> 01:46:19.060
...for making you
a Cyber-Newtype!

01:46:19.060 --> 01:46:23.680
If there's any humanity at all
left in you, you'll stop this!

01:46:23.680 --> 01:46:27.940
I was ordered to kill nine-tenths
of humanity, so l changed!

01:46:27.940 --> 01:46:30.110
That's nonsense, you machine!

01:46:33.320 --> 01:46:35.200
Cecily!

01:46:40.830 --> 01:46:42.870
I'm no machine.

01:46:42.870 --> 01:46:46.540
My ego was expanded to allow
me to carry out my duties!

01:46:48.170 --> 01:46:50.550
The escape pod isn't working...

01:46:55.970 --> 01:46:57.890
Frightened?

01:47:06.810 --> 01:47:09.110
I'm also capable
of brainwave control.

01:47:15.240 --> 01:47:19.620
I also operate machines
without using my hands or feet.

01:47:19.620 --> 01:47:21.660
You look down
on me like Nadia.

01:47:21.660 --> 01:47:24.700
Women are so
hard to manage!

01:47:24.700 --> 01:47:28.120
All of that is your fault!
You can't take off that mask!

01:47:28.330 --> 01:47:30.250
You still say that?

01:47:31.960 --> 01:47:33.500
What?

01:47:40.640 --> 01:47:43.100
How many are there?

01:47:46.140 --> 01:47:47.850
Cecily!

01:47:54.400 --> 01:47:57.150
Afterimages that have mass?

01:48:00.160 --> 01:48:01.660
You can't catch me!

01:48:04.540 --> 01:48:07.250
The afterimages
are drawing his fire?

01:48:07.460 --> 01:48:08.790
What?

01:48:12.170 --> 01:48:15.170
You want me
to use that, Cecily?

01:48:22.760 --> 01:48:25.220
It takes more than
a mobile suit engine...

01:48:25.470 --> 01:48:26.770
There!

01:48:29.940 --> 01:48:31.560
There?

01:48:39.490 --> 01:48:41.160
That won't stop me!

01:48:44.830 --> 01:48:46.910
ls he some kind of monster?

01:49:01.760 --> 01:49:05.300
There was a large
mobile suit force out here?

01:49:05.300 --> 01:49:07.060
- Look for them!
- Yes, sir!

01:49:15.730 --> 01:49:16.860
Cecily?

01:49:16.860 --> 01:49:18.570
Cecily!

01:49:18.570 --> 01:49:19.990
Where did you go?

01:49:19.990 --> 01:49:22.660
Where are you?
Where are you, Cecily?

01:49:22.660 --> 01:49:27.290
lf you die now, everything we
went through is meaningless!

01:49:34.170 --> 01:49:36.090
There was only one?

01:49:36.090 --> 01:49:40.210
This lone, incapacitated mobile
suit is the only one in the area?

01:49:40.210 --> 01:49:41.720
How can this be?

01:49:48.890 --> 01:49:51.180
Cecily, send up a signal flare!

01:49:51.180 --> 01:49:52.230
Where are you?

01:49:52.400 --> 01:49:54.440
Hey, l can use the radio again!

01:49:53.400 --> 01:49:54.440
Cecily?

01:49:54.440 --> 01:49:56.000
He's looking for Lady Berah?

01:49:56.000 --> 01:49:57.190
Respond!

01:49:57.190 --> 01:49:59.400
So you destroyed
the Rafflesia with that...

01:50:00.040 --> 01:50:01.150
Thank you for your trouble.

01:50:14.120 --> 01:50:15.420
Will we be okay?

01:50:15.420 --> 01:50:17.250
I can hear what
the captain's saying to them.

01:50:24.260 --> 01:50:27.680
l verified 200 refugees
on board the ship.

01:50:28.510 --> 01:50:30.350
All right, let's pull back.

01:50:30.350 --> 01:50:33.930
lt may be a trainer,
but it's still a military vessel.

01:50:33.930 --> 01:50:36.600
We should act like
the Bugs or the Rafflesia?

01:50:36.600 --> 01:50:38.190
No, but...

01:50:38.190 --> 01:50:40.860
Then we can let
one refugee ship go.

01:50:40.860 --> 01:50:42.110
Yes, sir.

01:50:42.110 --> 01:50:44.070
lt may be its mother ship.

01:50:44.240 --> 01:50:46.490
- What's that?
- No, it's nothing.

01:50:46.490 --> 01:50:49.160
Let's join the Dorel
team home in triumph!

01:50:49.160 --> 01:50:50.490
Yes, sir!

01:50:59.920 --> 01:51:02.510
Mobile suit formations...

01:51:02.510 --> 01:51:05.420
They're the ones who took out
the Fed's Moon reinforcements.

01:51:09.970 --> 01:51:12.220
l'll let you out in a bit.

01:51:12.220 --> 01:51:14.520
Look, isn't the Moon pretty?

01:51:14.520 --> 01:51:16.350
Seabook's still alive!

01:51:16.350 --> 01:51:18.230
What's Seabook yelling about?

01:51:18.230 --> 01:51:20.360
What happened to Cecily?

01:51:20.360 --> 01:51:23.480
Her Vigna Ghina was
destroyed, wasn't it?

01:51:24.940 --> 01:51:26.820
- Really?
- What?

01:51:26.820 --> 01:51:28.410
Cecily was thrown clear?

01:51:28.410 --> 01:51:29.740
ls that true?

01:51:29.740 --> 01:51:30.870
What?

01:51:30.870 --> 01:51:32.330
You saw it happen?

01:51:32.330 --> 01:51:36.580
Minovsky particles are thinning,
but my radar isn't working!

01:51:36.580 --> 01:51:40.290
You and the Space Ark use
your radar to look for her!

01:51:40.290 --> 01:51:42.420
It's not completely clear yet!

01:51:42.420 --> 01:51:45.880
It's littered with
machine fragments!

01:51:45.880 --> 01:51:48.090
That doesn't mean
we should forget her!

01:51:48.090 --> 01:51:50.340
Aren't we going to the Moon?

01:51:50.760 --> 01:51:52.810
We'll look for the castaway.

01:51:52.810 --> 01:51:55.270
360 degree scan, people!

01:51:55.270 --> 01:51:58.730
Cecily's still alive,
floating out there somewhere?

01:51:59.270 --> 01:52:01.150
Quiet, Kochun.

01:52:01.150 --> 01:52:03.070
The Moon's there...

01:52:03.070 --> 01:52:05.190
Frontier l's there...

01:52:05.190 --> 01:52:07.280
And the sun's over there...

01:52:07.280 --> 01:52:10.280
She would've gone this
way from the explosion...

01:52:10.280 --> 01:52:12.990
Seabook, you can look for her.

01:52:13.740 --> 01:52:14.910
Mom!

01:52:14.910 --> 01:52:18.710
You can overlay Psycommu
and radar coordinates.

01:52:22.170 --> 01:52:23.750
What do you mean?

01:52:23.750 --> 01:52:27.970
You know the F91 has a system
that responds to brainwaves, right?

01:52:27.970 --> 01:52:29.010
Sort of.

01:52:29.010 --> 01:52:30.470
Use that as a sensor!

01:52:30.470 --> 01:52:32.090
But how?

01:52:32.090 --> 01:52:36.060
Set the thermal sensor to
human body heat's wavelength...

01:52:36.060 --> 01:52:40.900
...pass that through the filter, and
connect it to your radar display.

01:52:40.900 --> 01:52:44.230
This should double
or triple the reception.

01:52:46.530 --> 01:52:49.320
But it depends
on your sensitivity.

01:52:49.320 --> 01:52:51.280
I have to sense her?

01:52:51.280 --> 01:52:52.570
Yes.

01:52:53.370 --> 01:52:55.740
It's the operator that matters.

01:52:55.740 --> 01:52:57.240
Well? Anything?

01:53:01.330 --> 01:53:04.290
But more than half
my cameras are gone!

01:53:04.290 --> 01:53:08.010
If you only focus on what
you see in front of you...

01:53:08.010 --> 01:53:09.340
...you'll never sense anything.

01:53:09.340 --> 01:53:11.930
It's useless!

01:53:11.930 --> 01:53:13.510
l can't sense anything!

01:53:13.510 --> 01:53:15.180
Stop acting like a child.

01:53:15.180 --> 01:53:18.060
Calm your mind and
focus your emotions.

01:53:18.600 --> 01:53:21.770
Empty your mind and
open your perceptions...

01:53:21.770 --> 01:53:25.270
...solely to the pulsing of
the soul drifting in space.

01:53:25.270 --> 01:53:29.780
The soul that wants only you
is calling out to you, isn't it?

01:53:35.740 --> 01:53:37.080
He's moving!

01:53:37.080 --> 01:53:38.200
Did you find her?

01:53:38.200 --> 01:53:39.700
Don't use the radio.

01:54:00.430 --> 01:54:04.900
Seabook, who else but you
can care as much for her?

01:54:04.900 --> 01:54:06.190
But...

01:54:06.190 --> 01:54:09.690
But l'm not sensing anything!

01:54:10.440 --> 01:54:12.150
Then draw her to you.

01:54:12.150 --> 01:54:13.650
You can do that, too.

01:54:13.650 --> 01:54:16.200
That's the power of human life.

01:54:16.740 --> 01:54:19.950
Draw her to me? But how?

01:54:24.580 --> 01:54:26.420
That light...

01:54:27.130 --> 01:54:28.290
Vernier!

01:54:28.290 --> 01:54:29.880
What? What happened?

01:54:29.880 --> 01:54:32.130
Did you sense Cecily?

01:54:32.130 --> 01:54:33.510
No.

01:54:33.510 --> 01:54:35.220
That's a flower!

01:54:35.220 --> 01:54:36.340
Cecily's flower!

01:54:36.340 --> 01:54:37.470
Cecily's flower?

01:54:37.470 --> 01:54:40.060
It's gotta be Cecily!

01:54:41.430 --> 01:54:43.340
You'll never make
it on one vernier!

01:55:39.120 --> 01:55:43.290
maru de kanashimi no kakera da wa

01:55:39.120 --> 01:55:43.290
Almost like shards of sorrow...

01:55:44.330 --> 01:55:45.790
Cecily?

01:55:44.330 --> 01:55:49.500
machi wo tozasu garasu iro no yuki

01:55:44.330 --> 01:55:49.500
...glass-colored snow hems the town in.

01:55:49.500 --> 01:55:54.090
ashita wo sagasu hitomi sae mo

01:55:49.500 --> 01:55:54.090
Even eyes that search for tomorrow...

01:55:54.590 --> 01:55:59.640
kumorasete yuku no yami no kanata

01:55:54.590 --> 01:55:59.640
...are dimmed by the depths of the darkness.

01:55:56.340 --> 01:55:58.090
Cecily!

01:55:59.640 --> 01:56:04.850
mishiranu chikara ni nagasarete

01:55:59.640 --> 01:56:04.850
Being swept along by an unfamiliar power...

01:56:04.850 --> 01:56:09.770
kokoro ga dokoka e hagureteku

01:56:04.850 --> 01:56:09.770
...the heart is led astray somewhere.

01:56:08.060 --> 01:56:09.140
Seabook?

01:56:10.060 --> 01:56:14.980
harisakesou na mune no oku de

01:56:10.060 --> 01:56:14.980
Deep within this heart that seems fit to burst...

01:56:14.980 --> 01:56:21.280
kodou dake ga tashika ni ikite iru

01:56:14.980 --> 01:56:21.280
...it's only the throbbing that is surely alive.

01:56:23.160 --> 01:56:28.080
hikaru kaze no naka

01:56:23.160 --> 01:56:28.080
Within the shining wind...

01:56:28.080 --> 01:56:32.000
kikoete kuru anata no koe

01:56:28.080 --> 01:56:32.000
...l can hear your voice.

01:56:33.540 --> 01:56:38.220
Pray don't break our peace forever...

01:56:38.220 --> 01:56:45.720
sono kagayaki wo shinjite iru

01:56:38.220 --> 01:56:45.720
...l believe in that brilliance.

01:56:59.900 --> 01:57:04.530
aoku kemuru suiheisen wo

01:56:59.900 --> 01:57:04.530
Because my eyes still remember...

01:57:05.160 --> 01:57:10.460
kono me wa mada oboete iru kara

01:57:05.160 --> 01:57:10.460
...that blue, hazy horizon.

01:57:10.460 --> 01:57:15.090
mabuta wo tojireba kaereru no

01:57:10.460 --> 01:57:15.090
lf l close my eyes, l can go back...

01:57:15.630 --> 01:57:20.670
atataka na jikan omoidetachi

01:57:15.630 --> 01:57:20.670
...to memories of those warm, happy hours.

01:57:20.670 --> 01:57:25.890
kurikaesu ayamachi ga itsumo

01:57:20.670 --> 01:57:25.890
Mistakes repeated again and again...

01:57:25.890 --> 01:57:31.020
orokana ikimono ni kaeteku

01:57:25.890 --> 01:57:31.020
...turn into foolish creatures.

01:57:31.020 --> 01:57:35.860
kizutsuku dake no ikikata demo

01:57:31.020 --> 01:57:35.860
Even my way of life is full of pain...

01:57:35.860 --> 01:57:42.530
namida wa sou yo kesshite misenai wa

01:57:35.860 --> 01:57:42.530
...but l'll never show any tears.

01:57:43.950 --> 01:57:49.040
hikaru kaze no naka

01:57:43.950 --> 01:57:49.040
Within the shining wind...

01:57:49.040 --> 01:57:54.540
hohoende iru anata ga iru

01:57:49.040 --> 01:57:54.540
...you're there smiling.

01:57:54.540 --> 01:57:59.340
Pray don't break our peace forever...

01:57:59.340 --> 01:58:07.640
sono mabushisa wo mitsumete iru

01:57:59.340 --> 01:58:07.640
...l gaze straight into that brilliance.

01:58:26.070 --> 01:58:31.160
hageshii itami wa dare no tame

01:58:26.070 --> 01:58:31.160
l think l've finally learned...

01:58:31.160 --> 01:58:36.540
sore ga yatto wakaru ki ga suru wa

01:58:31.160 --> 01:58:36.540
...who this intense pain is for.

01:58:36.540 --> 01:58:41.760
meguriaisou kiseki na no

01:58:36.540 --> 01:58:41.760
Our chance encounter was a miracle...

01:58:41.760 --> 01:58:46.720
ikuoku no hoshi ga samayou sora

01:58:41.760 --> 01:58:46.720
...just two of billions of stars wandering the sky.

01:58:46.720 --> 01:58:51.930
sayonara ga oshiete kureta no

01:58:46.720 --> 01:58:51.930
lt was our parting that taught...

01:58:51.930 --> 01:58:57.100
anata no hontou no yasashisa

01:58:51.930 --> 01:58:57.100
...me your true kindness.

01:58:57.100 --> 01:59:02.030
dare yori mo daiji na hito da to

01:58:57.100 --> 01:59:02.030
On any day, l can say with head held high...

01:59:02.030 --> 01:59:09.320
mune wo hatte ieru wa itsu no hi mo

01:59:02.030 --> 01:59:09.320
...that you mean more than anyone to me.

01:59:10.120 --> 01:59:15.120
hikaru kaze no naka

01:59:10.120 --> 01:59:15.120
Within the shining wind...

01:59:15.120 --> 01:59:20.670
hohoende iru anata ga iru

01:59:15.120 --> 01:59:20.670
...you're there smiling.

01:59:20.670 --> 01:59:25.550
Pray don't break our peace forever...

01:59:25.550 --> 01:59:33.020
sono mabushisa wo mitsumete iru

01:59:25.550 --> 01:59:33.020
...l gaze straight into that brilliance.

01:59:31.100 --> 01:59:35.930
Pray don't break our peace forever...

01:59:35.930 --> 01:59:46.070
atsui hitomi ni yakitsukete

01:59:35.930 --> 01:59:46.070
...its image burned into my passionate eyes.
